{"timestamp":"2026-09-05T01:00:30.629Z","ordinal":19555,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06cdc-629f-7b82-8a80-b940922d7571","turn_id":"01a06cdc-6399-7b30-9fa8-4b87f0cfba0e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8ab55ff2-3074-4552-9d69-410b1d4b7916","process_id":"68941","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat /Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/aa9e/evorto-stack-review/prefix-runtime-verification/post-replay-gates/independent12a-audit/README.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/aa9e/evorto","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat /Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/aa9e/evorto-stack-review/prefix-runtime-verification/post-replay-gates/independent12a-audit/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/aa9e/evorto-stack-review/prefix-runtime-verification/post-replay-gates/independent12a-audit/README.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# Independent nested 12a evidence audit\n\nThe retained nested evidence is internally consistent: 54 artifacts, 68 reference edges, all recorded digests, 22 historical ordinary gate records, and all 5,721 archived source-file hashes were checked. No missing artifact or digest mismatch remains. This is an integrity review, not a new gate execution or gate approval. Original receipts and logs were not edited.\n\nHistorical head `dab0f1d5cecd1a0656ad2e480dc41e637075400b` and replayed head `36f1e5b28f59b4512d0237ae89ae7e07cdf6eb13` have the same complete tree `c4513e5a659f4d3c98abd246cda6d271b98b3ca5`: all tracked paths, modes and blob identities match; Git diff is empty. The historical full archive digest also matches. That archive carries the original commit identity and must retain its original provenance.\n\n| Historical command | Verified final result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Retained `node typecheck.mjs` | 58 changed roots; 286 first-party sources reported; 0 diagnostics |\n| `bun run test:unit:server` | 204 files / 1,718 tests passed |\n| `bun run test:unit --watch=false` | 129 files / 974 tests passed |\n| `bun run test:integration:postgres:local` | 20 files / 152 tests passed |\n\nRaw logs, commands, exit status, before/after clean source identities and recorded tool paths/versions agree. The ordinary runner pins Node 24.15.0 and Bun 1.3.14; raw test logs identify Vitest 4.1.10. The locked dependency/config inputs are identical. Canonical file patterns independently enumerate exactly 204 server, 129 app and 20 PostgreSQL files. Both test configurations retain the complete-run reporter and disallow focused cases; raw final summaries report all collected cases passed. Earlier 4eb1 and 40fb attempts, including their failures and the stopped waiting supervisor, remain recorded and excluded from the final result.\n\nThe strict wrapper is HEAD-sensitive: it verifies the historical checkout and selects changed roots with explicit old base/head refs. I independently compared both historical and replayed stack edges; they yield the same 62 changed paths and exact 58 TypeScript roots. `strict-roots.json` records every root and source hash. The retained probe uses the actual tsconfig plus noEmit, node/bun/google.maps types and checkout rootDir, without added diagnostic filtering; canonical skipLibCheck remains. Compiler analysis is content-based once these inputs are fixed. No current-repository HEAD dependency was found in the full unit entry points: Git fixtures own temporary repositories, while revision tests supply explicit fixture revisions. PostgreSQL runner/environment/schema code does not read Git identity. Image/build identity is HEAD-sensitive and excluded from historical rebinding.\n\nPostgreSQL source/command/log/container identity agree. A successful canonical runner implies its mandatory PostgreSQL-major-17 check passed before schema reset/push. The historical cleanup receipt records zero URL-race tenants, idle transactions and active client queries on the same container at its stated time. It proves those counters only; it is not a container-removal, comprehensive database-empty or current-health receipt.\n\nEvidence limits remain explicit: the old strict probe/runner lacked a separately recorded historical digest, so this audit hashes the retained files without retroactive timestamp attestation; the 286-source compiler count is cross-checked from retained records, not recomputed by a new compilation. PostgreSQL engine patch/image digest and separately resolved PG Node/Bun executables were not recorded. A fresh short PG run at activation can resolve any stronger engine/cleanup requirement.\n\nRoot policy governs activation: only explicitly labelled historical strict, full unit and PostgreSQL content results are candidates. Frozen install, release, format, lint, clean-state, infrastructure, image and runtime acceptance remain fresh requirements. The proposed supplement still lists broader format/lint/infra reuse; activation must narrow it to root's policy. No old time, head, image, runtime or provider outcome may be labelled a fresh execution.\n\n`audit.json` binds every checked digest and limitation; `suite-file-census.json` and `strict-roots.json` provide exact file lists. `audit.py` performs only file/Git-object reads and writes this external report; no compiler, test, database, provider, image, ref or shared-source action ran.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# Independent nested 12a evidence audit\n\nThe retained nested evidence is internally consistent: 54 artifacts, 68 reference edges, all recorded digests, 22 historical ordinary gate records, and all 5,721 archived source-file hashes were checked. No missing artifact or digest mismatch remains. This is an integrity review, not a new gate execution or gate approval. Original receipts and logs were not edited.\n\nHistorical head `dab0f1d5cecd1a0656ad2e480dc41e637075400b` and replayed head `36f1e5b28f59b4512d0237ae89ae7e07cdf6eb13` have the same complete tree `c4513e5a659f4d3c98abd246cda6d271b98b3ca5`: all tracked paths, modes and blob identities match; Git diff is empty. The historical full archive digest also matches. That archive carries the original commit identity and must retain its original provenance.\n\n| Historical command | Verified final result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Retained `node typecheck.mjs` | 58 changed roots; 286 first-party sources reported; 0 diagnostics |\n| `bun run test:unit:server` | 204 files / 1,718 tests passed |\n| `bun run test:unit --watch=false` | 129 files / 974 tests passed |\n| `bun run test:integration:postgres:local` | 20 files / 152 tests passed |\n\nRaw logs, commands, exit status, before/after clean source identities and recorded tool paths/versions agree. The ordinary runner pins Node 24.15.0 and Bun 1.3.14; raw test logs identify Vitest 4.1.10. The locked dependency/config inputs are identical. Canonical file patterns independently enumerate exactly 204 server, 129 app and 20 PostgreSQL files. Both test configurations retain the complete-run reporter and disallow focused cases; raw final summaries report all collected cases passed. Earlier 4eb1 and 40fb attempts, including their failures and the stopped waiting supervisor, remain recorded and excluded from the final result.\n\nThe strict wrapper is HEAD-sensitive: it verifies the historical checkout and selects changed roots with explicit old base/head refs. I independently compared both historical and replayed stack edges; they yield the same 62 changed paths and exact 58 TypeScript roots. `strict-roots.json` records every root and source hash. The retained probe uses the actual tsconfig plus noEmit, node/bun/google.maps types and checkout rootDir, without added diagnostic filtering; canonical skipLibCheck remains. Compiler analysis is content-based once these inputs are fixed. No current-repository HEAD dependency was found in the full unit entry points: Git fixtures own temporary repositories, while revision tests supply explicit fixture revisions. PostgreSQL runner/environment/schema code does not read Git identity. Image/build identity is HEAD-sensitive and excluded from historical rebinding.\n\nPostgreSQL source/command/log/container identity agree. A successful canonical runner implies its mandatory PostgreSQL-major-17 check passed before schema reset/push. The historical cleanup receipt records zero URL-race tenants, idle transactions and active client queries on the same container at its stated time. It proves those counters only; it is not a container-removal, comprehensive database-empty or current-health receipt.\n\nEvidence limits remain explicit: the old strict probe/runner lacked a separately recorded historical digest, so this audit hashes the retained files without retroactive timestamp attestation; the 286-source compiler count is cross-checked from retained records, not recomputed by a new compilation. PostgreSQL engine patch/image digest and separately resolved PG Node/Bun executables were not recorded. A fresh short PG run at activation can resolve any stronger engine/cleanup requirement.\n\nRoot policy governs activation: only explicitly labelled historical strict, full unit and PostgreSQL content results are candidates. Frozen install, release, format, lint, clean-state, infrastructure, image and runtime acceptance remain fresh requirements. The proposed supplement still lists broader format/lint/infra reuse; activation must narrow it to root's policy. No old time, head, image, runtime or provider outcome may be labelled a fresh execution.\n\n`audit.json` binds every checked digest and limitation; `suite-file-census.json` and `strict-roots.json` provide exact file lists. `audit.py` performs only file/Git-object reads and writes this external report; no compiler, test, database, provider, image, ref or shared-source action ran.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3584},"formatted_output":"# Independent nested 12a evidence audit\n\nThe retained nested evidence is internally consistent: 54 artifacts, 68 reference edges, all recorded digests, 22 historical ordinary gate records, and all 5,721 archived source-file hashes were checked. No missing artifact or digest mismatch remains. This is an integrity review, not a new gate execution or gate approval. Original receipts and logs were not edited.\n\nHistorical head `dab0f1d5cecd1a0656ad2e480dc41e637075400b` and replayed head `36f1e5b28f59b4512d0237ae89ae7e07cdf6eb13` have the same complete tree `c4513e5a659f4d3c98abd246cda6d271b98b3ca5`: all tracked paths, modes and blob identities match; Git diff is empty. The historical full archive digest also matches. That archive carries the original commit identity and must retain its original provenance.\n\n| Historical command | Verified final result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Retained `node typecheck.mjs` | 58 changed roots; 286 first-party sources reported; 0 diagnostics |\n| `bun run test:unit:server` | 204 files / 1,718 tests passed |\n| `bun run test:unit --watch=false` | 129 files / 974 tests passed |\n| `bun run test:integration:postgres:local` | 20 files / 152 tests passed |\n\nRaw logs, commands, exit status, before/after clean source identities and recorded tool paths/versions agree. The ordinary runner pins Node 24.15.0 and Bun 1.3.14; raw test logs identify Vitest 4.1.10. The locked dependency/config inputs are identical. Canonical file patterns independently enumerate exactly 204 server, 129 app and 20 PostgreSQL files. Both test configurations retain the complete-run reporter and disallow focused cases; raw final summaries report all collected cases passed. Earlier 4eb1 and 40fb attempts, including their failures and the stopped waiting supervisor, remain recorded and excluded from the final result.\n\nThe strict wrapper is HEAD-sensitive: it verifies the historical checkout and selects changed roots with explicit old base/head refs. I independently compared both historical and replayed stack edges; they yield the same 62 changed paths and exact 58 TypeScript roots. `strict-roots.json` records every root and source hash. The retained probe uses the actual tsconfig plus noEmit, node/bun/google.maps types and checkout rootDir, without added diagnostic filtering; canonical skipLibCheck remains. Compiler analysis is content-based once these inputs are fixed. No current-repository HEAD dependency was found in the full unit entry points: Git fixtures own temporary repositories, while revision tests supply explicit fixture revisions. PostgreSQL runner/environment/schema code does not read Git identity. Image/build identity is HEAD-sensitive and excluded from historical rebinding.\n\nPostgreSQL source/command/log/container identity agree. A successful canonical runner implies its mandatory PostgreSQL-major-17 check passed before schema reset/push. The historical cleanup receipt records zero URL-race tenants, idle transactions and active client queries on the same container at its stated time. It proves those counters only; it is not a container-removal, comprehensive database-empty or current-health receipt.\n\nEvidence limits remain explicit: the old strict probe/runner lacked a separately recorded historical digest, so this audit hashes the retained files without retroactive timestamp attestation; the 286-source compiler count is cross-checked from retained records, not recomputed by a new compilation. PostgreSQL engine patch/image digest and separately resolved PG Node/Bun executables were not recorded. A fresh short PG run at activation can resolve any stronger engine/cleanup requirement.\n\nRoot policy governs activation: only explicitly labelled historical strict, full unit and PostgreSQL content results are candidates. Frozen install, release, format, lint, clean-state, infrastructure, image and runtime acceptance remain fresh requirements. The proposed supplement still lists broader format/lint/infra reuse; activation must narrow it to root's policy. No old time, head, image, runtime or provider outcome may be labelled a fresh execution.\n\n`audit.json` binds every checked digest and limitation; `suite-file-census.json` and `strict-roots.json` provide exact file lists. `audit.py` performs only file/Git-object reads and writes this external report; no compiler, test, database, provider, image, ref or shared-source action ran.\n"},"started_at_ms":1788570030629,"completed_at_ms":1788570030629}}
