{"timestamp":"2026-09-05T01:22:11.370Z","ordinal":20062,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a06f28-ab2a-7d20-9763-233bc4698874","call_id":"call_Ir54VJ473527nhs4hhItlgN2","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"0d5ea3\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00000475,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2693,\"output\":\"        closeRegistrationTime: new Date('2100-01-01T23:00:00.000Z'),\\n        eventId: optionfulUnrestrictedId,\\n        id: optionfulUnrestrictedOptionId,\\n        isPaid: false,\\n        openRegistrationTime: new Date('2099-12-01T00:00:00.000Z'),\\n        organizingRegistration: false,\\n        price: 0,\\n        registrationMode: 'fcfs',\\n        roleIds: [],\\n        spots: 20,\\n        title: 'Unrestricted participant',\\n      },\\n      {\\n        closeRegistrationTime: new Date('2100-01-01T23:00:00.000Z'),\\n        eventId: optionfulDefaultRoleId,\\n        id: optionfulDefaultRoleOptionId,\\n        isPaid: false,\\n        openRegistrationTime: new Date('2099-12-01T00:00:00.000Z'),\\n        organizingRegistration: false,\\n        price: 0,\\n        registrationMode: 'fcfs',\\n        roleIds: [defaultRoleId],\\n        spots: 20,\\n        title: 'Default-role participant',\\n      },\\n      {\\n        closeRegistrationTime: new Date('2100-01-01T23:00:00.000Z'),\\n        eventId: draftRestrictedId,\\n        id: draftRestrictedOptionId,\\n        isPaid: false,\\n        openRegistrationTime: new Date('2099-12-01T00:00:00.000Z'),\\n        organizingRegistration: false,\\n        price: 0,\\n        registrationMode: 'fcfs',\\n        roleIds: [matchingRoleId],\\n        spots: 20,\\n        title: 'Restricted draft participant',\\n      },\\n    ]);\\n  });\\n\\n  afterAll(async () => {\\n    const databaseToClean = cleanupDatabase;\\n    const poolToEnd = cleanupPool;\\n    cleanupDatabase = undefined;\\n    cleanupPool = undefined;\\n    const failures: unknown[] = [];\\n    for (const cleanup of [\\n      ...(databaseToClean\\n        ? [\\n            () =>\\n              databaseToClean\\n                .delete(platformAuditEntries)\\n                .where(\\n                  inArray(platformAuditEntries.targetTenantId, [\\n                    tenantId,\\n                    otherTenantId,\\n                  ]),\\n                ),\\n            () =>\\n              databaseToClean\\n                .delete(eventRegistrationOptions)\\n                .where(\\n                  inArray(eventRegistrationOptions.id, [\\n                    optionfulMatchingOptionId,\\n                    optionfulUnrestrictedOptionId,\\n                    optionfulDefaultRoleOptionId,\\n                    draftRestrictedOptionId,\\n                  ]),\\n                ),\\n            () =>\\n              databaseToClean\\n                .delete(eventInstances)\\n                .where(inArray(eventInstances.id, eventIds)),\\n            () =>\\n              databaseToClean\\n                .delete(eventTemplates)\\n                .where(\\n                  inArray(eventTemplates.id, [templateId, otherTemplateId]),\\n                ),\\n            () =>\\n              databaseToClean\\n                .delete(eventTemplateCategories)\\n                .where(\\n                  inArray(eventTemplateCategories.id, [\\n                    categoryId,\\n                    otherCategoryId,\\n                  ]),\\n                ),\\n            () =>\\n              databaseToClean\\n                .delete(rolesToTenantUsers)\\n                .where(\\n                  inArray(rolesToTenantUsers.tenantId, [\\n                    tenantId,\\n                    otherTenantId,\\n                  ]),\\n                ),\\n            () =>\\n              databaseToClean\\n                .delete(usersToTenants)\\n                .where(\\n                  inArray(usersToTenants.tenantId, [tenantId, otherTenantId]),\\n                ),\\n            () =>\\n              databaseToClean\\n                .delete(roles)\\n                .where(inArray(roles.tenantId, [tenantId, otherTenantId])),\\n            () =>\\n              databaseToClean.delete(users).where(inArray(users.id, userIds)),\\n            () =>\\n              databaseToClean\\n                .delete(tenants)\\n                .where(inArray(tenants.id, [tenantId, otherTenantId])),\\n          ]\\n        : []),\\n      () => poolToEnd?.end(),\\n    ]) {\\n      try {\\n        await cleanup();\\n      } catch (error) {\\n        failures.push(error);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (failures.length > 0) {\\n      throw new AggregateError(\\n        failures,\\n        'Announcement discovery fixture cleanup failed',\\n        { cause: failures[0] },\\n      );\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  it('keeps announcement targeting separate from option eligibility and preserves direct links', async () => {\\n    expect(listedEventIds(await runEventList(anonymousContext))).toEqual(\\n      [optionfulDefaultRoleId, optionfulUnrestrictedId].toSorted(),\\n    );\\n\\n    const matchingContext = authenticatedContext({\\n      roleIds: [matchingRoleId],\\n      userId: matchingUserId,\\n    });\\n    expect(listedEventIds(await runEventList(matchingContext))).toEqual(\\n      [\\n        matchingAnnouncementId,\\n        optionfulMatchingId,\\n        optionfulUnrestrictedId,\\n      ].toSorted(),\\n    );\\n\\n    const nonmatchingContext = authenticatedContext({\\n      roleIds: [nonmatchingRoleId],\\n      userId: nonmatchingUserId,\\n    });\\n    expect(listedEventIds(await runEventList(nonmatchingContext))).toEqual([\\n      optionfulUnrestrictedId,\\n    ]);\\n\\n    const rolelessContext = authenticatedContext({\\n      roleIds: [],\\n      userId: matchingUserId,\\n      id: draftRestrictedId,\\n      registrationOptionsHiddenByEligibility: false,\\n    });\\n    expect(draft.registrationOptions.map((option) => option.id)).toEqual([\\n      draftRestrictedOptionId,\\n    ]);\\n    expect(draft.registrationOptions[0]).not.toHaveProperty('roleIds');\\n\\n    const approved = await runFindOne(draftViewerContext, optionfulMatchingId);\\n    expect(approved).toMatchObject({\\n      registrationOptions: [],\\n      registrationOptionsHiddenByEligibility: true,\\n    });\\n  });\\n\\n  it('serializes platform announcement updates with role deletion', async () => {\\n    const foreignRoleUpdate = await runPlatformAnnouncementDiscoveryUpdate(\\n      raceAnnouncementId,\\n      [otherTenantRoleId],\\n    );\\n    expect(foreignRoleUpdate).toMatchObject({\\n      error: {\\n        _tag: 'RpcBadRequestError',\\n        reason: 'invalidAnnouncementRole',\\n      },\\n      status: 'failure',\\n    });\\n\\n    const optionfulUpdate = await runPlatformAnnouncementDiscoveryUpdate(\\n      optionfulMatchingId,\\n      [],\\n    );\\n    expect(optionfulUpdate).toMatchObject({\\n      error: {\\n        _tag: 'RpcBadRequestError',\\n        reason: 'announcementRolesRequireOptionlessEvent',\\n      },\\n      status: 'failure',\\n    });\\n\\n    const lockClient = await pool.connect();\\n    let lockReleased = false;\\n    let discardLockClient = false;\\n    const failures: unknown[] = [];\\n    const operations: Promise<unknown>[] = [];\\n    const workers: { name: string; settled: boolean }[] = [];\\n    const recordFailure = (error: unknown) => {\\n      if (!failures.includes(error)) failures.push(error);\\n    };\\n    const observeWorker = <Result>(\\n      name: string,\\n      operation: Promise<Result>,\\n    ) => {\\n      const worker = { name, settled: false };\\n      workers.push(worker);\\n      operations.push(operation);\\n      // Observe immediately, before waiting for either lock barrier.\\n      void operation.then(\\n        () => {\\n          worker.settled = true;\\n        },\\n        (error: unknown) => {\\n          worker.settled = true;\\n          recordFailure(error);\\n        },\\n      );\\n      return operation;\\n    };\\n    const ensureWorkersUnsettled = () => {\\n      if (failures.length > 0) throw failures[0];\\n      const completed = workers.find((worker) => worker.settled);\\n      if (completed) {\\n        throw new Error(\\n          `${completed.name} completed before its role-graph lock was observed`,\\n        );\\n      }\\n    };\\n    try {\\n      await lockTenantRoleGraph(lockClient, tenantId);\\n      const updatePromise = observeWorker(\\n        'Announcement update',\\n        runPlatformAnnouncementDiscoveryUpdate(raceAnnouncementId, [\\n          raceRoleId,\\n        ]),\\n      );\\n      await waitForBlockedRoleGraphLocks(pool, 1, ensureWorkersUnsettled);\\n      const deletePromise = observeWorker('Role deletion', runRoleDeletion());\\n      await waitForBlockedRoleGraphLocks(pool, 2, ensureWorkersUnsettled);\\n      await lockClient.query('COMMIT');\\n      lockReleased = true;\\n\\n      const [updateResult, deleteResult] = await Promise.all([\\n        updatePromise,\\n        deletePromise,\\n      ]);\\n\\n      const [storedEvent] = await database\\n        .select({ announcementRoleIds: eventInstances.announcementRoleIds })\\n        .from(eventInstances)\\n        .where(eq(eventInstances.id, raceAnnouncementId));\\n      const storedRole = await database.query.roles.findFirst({\\n        columns: { id: true },\\n        where: { id: raceRoleId, tenantId },\\n      });\\n      const auditEntries = await database\\n        .select({ action: platformAuditEntries.action })\\n        .from(platformAuditEntries)\\n        .where(\\n          and(\\n            eq(platformAuditEntries.targetTenantId, tenantId),\\n            inArray(platformAuditEntries.action, [\\n              'event.updateAnnouncementDiscovery',\\n              'role.delete',\\n            ]),\\n          ),\\n        );\\n\\n      if (updateResult.status === 'success') {\\n        expect(deleteResult).toMatchObject({\\n          error: {\\n            _tag: 'RpcBadRequestError',\\n            reason: 'roleInUseByEventAnnouncement',\\n          },\\n          status: 'failure',\\n        });\\n        expect(storedEvent?.announcementRoleIds).toEqual([raceRoleId]);\\n        expect(storedRole).toEqual({ id: raceRoleId });\\n        expect(auditEntries).toEqual([\\n          { action: 'event.updateAnnouncementDiscovery' },\\n        ]);\\n      } else {\\n        expect(updateResult.error).toMatchObject({\\n          _tag: 'RpcBadRequestError',\\n          reason: 'invalidAnnouncementRole',\\n        });\\n        expect(deleteResult).toEqual({ status: 'success' });\\n        expect(storedEvent?.announcementRoleIds).toEqual([]);\\n        expect(storedRole).toBeUndefined();\\n        expect(auditEntries).toEqual([{ action: 'role.delete' }]);\\n      }\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      recordFailure(error);\\n    } finally {\\n      if (!lockReleased) {\\n        try {\\n          await lockClient.query('ROLLBACK');\\n          lockReleased = true;\\n        } catch (error) {\\n          discardLockClient = true;\\n          recordFailure(error);\\n        }\\n      }\\n      try {\\n        // Destroy a client after a failed rollback so it cannot retain the lock.\\n        lockClient.release(discardLockClient);\\n      } catch (error) {\\n        recordFailure(error);\\n      }\\n      const settlements = await Promise.allSettled(operations);\\n      for (const settlement of settlements) {\\n        if (settlement.status === 'rejected') recordFailure(settlement.reason);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (failures.length > 0) {\\n      throw new AggregateError(\\n        failures,\\n        'Announcement discovery role-lock scenario failed',\\n        { cause: failures[0] },\\n      );\\n    }\\n  });\\n});\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"e4df38\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000004667,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":7382,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 7382)\\nTotal output lines: 41\\n\\nlayer17a-event-list-review/final-parent-rebind-review/final-acceptance.json\\nlayer17a-event-list-review/final-parent-rebind-review/overlap-map.json\\n| F-194 | Medium   | Event creation displays an editable ESNcard price but submits the template price instead.                                                                                                                             | Persist the submitted event price, including zero or removal, without changing the template.                                                                                                      | In progress: UI, contract, server, unit tests, journey, and guide updated; runtime proof pending.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\\n| F-195 | High     | A same-digest staging retry can bypass a previously failed schema application.                                                                                                                                        | Reconcile schema before releasing worker and web on every attempt.                                                                                                                                | In progress: workflow repaired; actual-step fake-command regression passes; final runtime gates pending.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\\n| F-196 | Medium   | Built-in HTTP tracing records raw URLs and queries alongside sanitized application traces.                                                                                                                            | Suppress the built-in request trace while retaining the sanitized trace.                                                                                                                          | In progress: repair and composed tracing regression pass; integrated gates pending.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\\n| F-197 | High     | Receipt promotion can leave permanent evidence objects without a tracked destination after finalization fails.                                                                                                        | Record the destination before writing it, preserving recovery through ambiguous database/storage outcomes.                                                                                        | In progress: promotion repair and failure/retry coverage implemented; final-layer storage/concurrency proof pending.                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\\n| F-198 | High     | Expired transfer offers still block ticket operations, and revised deadlines are not reapplied.                                                                                                                       | Recheck current transfer limits and expire inactive offers while preserving unresolved payment holds.                                                                                             | In progress: guards, reads, and regressions updated; integrated payment/concurrency proof pending.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\\n| F-199 | Medium   | Publishing new onboarding requirements leaves the publishing author on an access-error page.                                                                                                                          | Send the author through current onboarding and return to its settings page.                                                                                                                       | In progress: redirect, regression, journey, and guide updated; runtime proof pending.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\\n| F-200 | Medium   | Wildcard permission checks omit concrete capability dependencies and hide permitted navigation.                                                                                                                       | Expand tenant permissions and dependencies consistently while keeping platform authority separate.                                                                                                | In progress: resolver and navigation regressions pass; integrated role journeys pending.                                                                                              …4682 tokens truncated…   | Add-on handout details are blocked after ticket ownership transfers while a refund is pending or failed, even though ordinary use is allowed.                                                                         | Use the existing ownership-handoff blocking states for reads and preserve tenant, owner and expiration checks.                                                                                    | Resolved: the read guard and six PostgreSQL status cases pass the full 123-test database suite. Current owner, tenant and expiration checks remain enforced; refund and handout mutation policies are unchanged.                                                                                                                                  |\\n| F-227 | Medium   | Create-event-from-template checks paid sign-up options but omits paid add-ons copied from the template when payment setup is unavailable.                                                                             | Block submission with an explanation for any copied paid option or add-on while retaining every saved price.                                                                                      | Resolved in assembly 4dd644: copied paid add-ons block submission without payment setup, with six rendered cases and all 1,172 app tests passing. The full 167-test functional run proves blocking, payment restoration and unchanged copied prices.                                                                                              |\\n| F-228 | Medium   | Unknown mutation failures claim that nothing changed; successful saves/imports followed by failed page updates or navigation are also described as failed, and platform template saves can mark later edits as saved. | Explain unconfirmed outcomes and current-state checks, distinguish confirmed writes from failed follow-up work, preserve submitted snapshots and keep submission blocked until follow-up settles. | In progress: all nine authoring components, profile/card operations and the home/offline wording corrections pass all 1,674 server tests, 1,342 app tests, strict typing and 123 PostgreSQL tests. Fresh runtime and Browser acceptance remain pending. Lost-response cases are client simulations.                                               |\\n| F-229 | Low      | The missing-file receipt documentation screenshot retains the previous receipt approval success notification.                                                                                                         | Prove the previous matching success notice has disappeared before capturing the next documented receipt state.                                                                                    | In progress: the producer retains its approval, URL, database and email assertions and adds an exact notification-absence check. Fresh complete publication and visual verification are pending.                                                                                                                                                  |\\n| F-230 | Medium   | A failed later event-list page hides already loaded events and makes its recovery controls unreachable; the previous fixture combined impossible query states.                                                        | Keep retained event links visible after a later-page failure and let Load more retry that page using real query-state coverage.                                                                   | In progress: the retained-page correction and real infinite-query failure/retry case pass the complete 1,308-test app suite. Fresh runtime and Browser verification remain pending.                                                                                                                                                               |\\n| F-231 | Medium   | Removing a choice, question or add-on can crash the event editor because row tracking reads a removed Signal Forms field.                                                                                             | Track stable field identities and preserve surviving values, references and the single graph save after public removal.                                                                           | In progress: stable field tracking and three public removal/save regressions pass the complete 1,342-test app suite and strict checking. Surviving values, references and one graph save are preserved. Fresh runtime acceptance remains pending.                                                                                                 |\\n| F-232 | Medium   | Home-organization changes write unused cache keys, and overlapping home/profile saves can overwrite each other’s newer fields from captured snapshots.                                                                | Update the actual endpoint caches using their current matching-user values and change only the fields owned by each action.                                                                       | In progress: endpoint cache keys and current-value updates pass the complete 1,342-test app suite. Four real component cases cover native home success, both overlap orders and an old response against another user’s cache. Fresh runtime acceptance remains pending.                                                                           |\\n\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a06cdc-6399-7b30-9fa8-4b87f0cfba0e","create_time":1788571331.370351}}}
