re deletes a fixed named role and unconditionally resets shared RLS settings.                                                                                                   | Use uniquely owned role and policy objects within one transaction, reject pre-existing RLS state, and restore the original state through rollback.                                                | Resolved: uniquely owned transaction-scoped role/policy and nested-rollback preservation regression pass the full PostgreSQL suite. Readback confirms original tenant RLS flags and zero fixture roles or policies.                                                                                                                               |\n-| F-225 | Medium   | Member check-in uses a timestamp captured before lock waits and can remain eligible after the existing closing deadline.                                                                                              | Read the existing check-in clock after the registration and event locks, preserving the current opening and closing window.                                                                       | Resolved: check-in reads its clock after both locks. The actual SQL-adapter lock-wait regression passes in the full 1,674-test server suite; the original opening and closing policy is preserved.                                                                                                                                                |\n-| F-226 | Medium   | Add-on handout details are blocked after ticket ownership transfers while a refund is pending or failed, even though ordinary use is allowed.                                                                         | Use the existing ownership-handoff blocking states for reads and preserve tenant, owner and expiration checks.                                                                                    | Resolved: the read guard and six PostgreSQL status cases pass the full 123-t