{"timestamp":"2026-09-05T01:33:38.440Z","ordinal":20400,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06cdc-629f-7b82-8a80-b940922d7571","turn_id":"01a06cdc-6399-7b30-9fa8-4b87f0cfba0e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-731da72a-94a5-434e-b0a1-ce10eacb9e98","process_id":"8791","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat pr-drafts/02-local-runtime.body.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/aa9e/evorto-stack-review","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat pr-drafts/02-local-runtime.body.md","name":"02-local-runtime.body.md","path":"pr-drafts/02-local-runtime.body.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"Make the sample-data reset and all tenant seed writes commit in one transaction, so a late failure restores prior data and cannot mark a partial seed complete. Require complete tenant, role and registration context, and reject non-local database targets before local schema operations connect.\n\nLocal database and Docker mutations acquire a lease for their Compose project, preventing concurrent resets or service changes. Ordinary Docker operations have watchdogs and report failures; setup ensures the disposable integration database exists, packages the pinned Stripe listener script, and assigns Mailpit a worktree-specific loopback port. Application schema shapes are unchanged.\n\nValidation at `f58a50b3`: frozen install, release checks, lint/format, full server (1,394 tests), app (802 tests), PostgreSQL 17 (55 tests), Terraform validation/config scanning, and the production image build/runtime/maps/SBOM/current strict scan all pass. The image has zero HIGH/CRITICAL findings, including unfixed vulnerabilities. Authenticated E2E and documentation acceptance are tracked separately.\n\nThe validation above belongs to historical head `f58a50b3`. Current head `08806f0b` has a changed Stripe test helper and requires fresh ordinary, functional and documentation checks.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"Make the sample-data reset and all tenant seed writes commit in one transaction, so a late failure restores prior data and cannot mark a partial seed complete. Require complete tenant, role and registration context, and reject non-local database targets before local schema operations connect.\n\nLocal database and Docker mutations acquire a lease for their Compose project, preventing concurrent resets or service changes. Ordinary Docker operations have watchdogs and report failures; setup ensures the disposable integration database exists, packages the pinned Stripe listener script, and assigns Mailpit a worktree-specific loopback port. Application schema shapes are unchanged.\n\nValidation at `f58a50b3`: frozen install, release checks, lint/format, full server (1,394 tests), app (802 tests), PostgreSQL 17 (55 tests), Terraform validation/config scanning, and the production image build/runtime/maps/SBOM/current strict scan all pass. The image has zero HIGH/CRITICAL findings, including unfixed vulnerabilities. Authenticated E2E and documentation acceptance are tracked separately.\n\nThe validation above belongs to historical head `f58a50b3`. Current head `08806f0b` has a changed Stripe test helper and requires fresh ordinary, functional and documentation checks.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3625},"formatted_output":"Make the sample-data reset and all tenant seed writes commit in one transaction, so a late failure restores prior data and cannot mark a partial seed complete. Require complete tenant, role and registration context, and reject non-local database targets before local schema operations connect.\n\nLocal database and Docker mutations acquire a lease for their Compose project, preventing concurrent resets or service changes. Ordinary Docker operations have watchdogs and report failures; setup ensures the disposable integration database exists, packages the pinned Stripe listener script, and assigns Mailpit a worktree-specific loopback port. Application schema shapes are unchanged.\n\nValidation at `f58a50b3`: frozen install, release checks, lint/format, full server (1,394 tests), app (802 tests), PostgreSQL 17 (55 tests), Terraform validation/config scanning, and the production image build/runtime/maps/SBOM/current strict scan all pass. The image has zero HIGH/CRITICAL findings, including unfixed vulnerabilities. Authenticated E2E and documentation acceptance are tracked separately.\n\nThe validation above belongs to historical head `f58a50b3`. Current head `08806f0b` has a changed Stripe test helper and requires fresh ordinary, functional and documentation checks.\n"},"started_at_ms":1788572018440,"completed_at_ms":1788572018440}}
