{"timestamp":"2026-09-05T01:38:08.201Z","ordinal":20517,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a06cdc-629f-7b82-8a80-b940922d7571","turn_id":"01a06cdc-6399-7b30-9fa8-4b87f0cfba0e","session_id":"01a06cdc-629f-7b82-8a80-b940922d7571","root_turn_id":"01a06cdc-6399-7b30-9fa8-4b87f0cfba0e","response_id":"resp_0c5872428dbc2885016a9b727a1ec887d28fa2431a02cd177c","usage":{"input_tokens":169556,"cached_input_tokens":169344,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":244,"reasoning_output_tokens":0,"total_tokens":169800},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":293775015,"cached_input_tokens":289175680,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":943043,"reasoning_output_tokens":320534,"total_tokens":294718058},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":293775015,"cached_input_tokens":289175680,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":943043,"reasoning_output_tokens":320534,"total_tokens":294718058}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-05T01:38:08.212Z","ordinal":20518,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06cdc-629f-7b82-8a80-b940922d7571","turn_id":"01a06cdc-6399-7b30-9fa8-4b87f0cfba0e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-71da7eee-43f1-4c13-8d71-521fdbed2067","process_id":"75094","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat prefix-runtime-verification/result-verifier-proposal/README.md && cat prefix-runtime-verification/result-verifier-proposal/verify_results.py"],"cwd":"file:///Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/aa9e/evorto-stack-review","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat prefix-runtime-verification/result-verifier-proposal/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"prefix-runtime-verification/result-verifier-proposal/README.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat prefix-runtime-verification/result-verifier-proposal/verify_results.py","name":"verify_results.py","path":"prefix-runtime-verification/result-verifier-proposal/verify_results.py"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# Prefix result verifier proposal\n\n`verify_results.py` verifies saved successful source, image and normal v2 runtime receipts. It does not execute gates, approve a prefix, inspect current processes/services, change refs, or repair evidence. Root review is required before operational use.\n\nRun with an explicit input manifest and a **new** output filename:\n\n```sh\npython3 prefix-runtime-verification/result-verifier-proposal/verify_results.py \\\n  --input prefix-runtime-verification/result-verifier-proposal/inputs/successful-01-v2.json \\\n  --output /absolute/path/to/a/new/result.json\n```\n\nThe output is `verified` with exit 0 only if every requested stage passes. Unknown formats, missing bindings, failed receipts, mismatched hashes and unsupported commands fail with exit 1. Existing output files are never replaced. Only read-only `git rev-parse` and `git show` subprocesses are used; the active checkout can belong to another prefix.\n\n## Input and checks\n\nThe example manifest supplies `reviewRoot`, `gitRepository`, full `head`/`tree`, and explicit `{path, sha256}` descriptors. `source` is required; `image`, `combined` and `runtime` may be added as their actual evidence becomes available. Image requires its source-evidence descriptor; combined requires image; runtime requires combined. Relative paths resolve within the review artifact root. Rebind the manifest to each exact prefix; never relabel a historical result.\n\n- **Source:** committed head/tree/parent; clean recorded before/after identities; pinned Node 24.15.0/Bun 1.3.14; invocation, runner and reviewed ownership-helper hashes; exact ordered invocation commands with no missing/extra gates; zero exits and absent command groups; raw-log hash/size; canonical package scripts and declared source/probe hashes. Both full Vitest summaries must occur once with positive equal passed/collected counts and no incomplete/retry/error summary. The actual layer 15 `types` and `tooling-lint` commands are supported through its declared probes, strict root set/options and diagnostic artifacts. Unknown extra command names fail.\n- **Image:** successful canonical command, exact revision tag, strict unfixed/update flags, clean source, positive tag absence before/after, completed builds and absent process group. The raw runtime-size line and complete wrapped Trivy table are parsed; every target must report zero findings. Exported manifest/config and all parsed values must match the root review and combined evidence. Two reviewed image-check script hashes are pinned because their source-map and SPDX nonempty checks are silent. If either script changes, obtain a source review and update the allowlist deliberately.\n- **PostgreSQL prerequisite:** exact identity, full unselected canonical command with exit 0, complete raw Vitest counts, same cleanup container, and all recorded scoped cleanup counters zero. The existing standalone PG receipt does not record a process group; the result explicitly leaves that proof uncertified.\n- **Runtime:** only `status: passed` from the reviewed v2 runner; exact immutable plan snapshot, inventory, admitted `layerLabel`/canonical scripts, readiness approval and combined prerequisite; exact checkout/install/full functional/full docs sequence; each raw-log hash/size and complete Playwright summary; runtime project/checkout/container/image/readiness identities; normal supervisor exit, group absence, empty resources and released ports. Failed layer 00 plus its exceptional cleanup supplement is deliberately unsupported. Preparation failures before execution do not become test retries; acceptance still requires the later actual successful receipt and exact accepted plan.\n\nAll bound raw logs in this prefix's supplied receipt chain are rehashed, including PostgreSQL and runtime-supervisor logs. The helper does not repeat the separate historical inventory audit across other prefixes. Recorded cleanup and source snapshots are evidence of the original run, not a fresh live-state census. It does not claim exported temporary archives still exist after canonical cleanup.\n\n## Offline comparison\n\n`dry-run-01/final.json` verifies the unchanged successful 01 records: **33 evidence files / 15 raw logs**, server **168 files / 1,351 tests**, app **111 / 802**, PG **14 / 55**, functional **151**, docs **52**, runtime image **95,708,630 bytes**, **297 targets / 0 HIGH or CRITICAL findings**. No application/provider/DB/runtime/compile command was run.\n\n`compare_offline.py` uses the real 01 logs and in-memory alterations. Its 17 rejection cases cover partial/duplicate/mismatched summaries, retry/flaky output, unknown/unscanned Trivy output, wrong identity, dirty source, changed hash, nonzero exit, live groups, unresolved EPERM and a failed runtime with otherwise green tests. The original evidence is never edited. The supplemental layer 15 parsers are source-adapted to its current invocation; fresh layer 15 outputs are still pending and are not claimed verified here.\n\nEarlier dry-run outputs remain: attempt 1 rejected a wrapped Trivy row until the exact continuation format was supported; attempt 2 rejected a newly changed live runtime plan. The corrected input uses root's immutable `plan-replayed-v2-before02.json`, whose hash exactly matches the 01 execution receipt. Attempts 3/4 and final passed. These are verifier development runs, never application test retries.\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Offline receipt verifier. Reads evidence/Git objects; never runs a gate or repairs evidence.\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\n\nTOOLS = {\"node\": \"v24.15.0\", \"bun\": \"1.3.14\"}\nOWNERSHIP_SHA = \"820f0fdd78f77d8cd3dc98586d661b58c1b86d10847c9b2b3d07d1f4253b2215\"\nRUNTIME_V2_SHA = \"b12d86b81a1e66ad8b3777deb5c62a74a8606ec39d925b66a6ab41ab5c3f65c2\"\n# Changes to these two silent-check scripts need a new source review, not substring guesses.\nIMAGE_CHECKS = {\n    \"ops/scaleway/verify-image-security.sh\": \"f56ca53d08227eb0623f2b32954aadc39ccdb09cbb16627a27682c23a0eb1df9\",\n    \"ops/scaleway/verify-runtime-image.sh\": \"d2e887a8481baaa9e787eb443ff23cc3f0550fe1e905ff1e6faae82c5770f972\",\n}\nSOURCE_COMMANDS = {\n    \"install\": [\"bun\", \"install\", \"--frozen-lockfile\"],\n    \"release\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"release:validate\"],\n    \"format\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"format:check\"],\n    \"lint\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"lint\"],\n    \"clean-diff\": [\"git\", \"diff\", \"--exit-code\"],\n    \"server\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"test:unit:server\"],\n    \"app\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"test:unit\"],\n    \"infra\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"infra:check\"],\n}\nRUNTIME_COMMANDS = {\n    \"install\": SOURCE_COMMANDS[\"install\"],\n    \"runtime\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"docker:webserver\"],\n    \"functional\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"test:e2e\"],\n    \"documentation\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"test:e2e:docs\"],\n}\nANSI = re.compile(r\"\\x1b\\[[0-?]*[ -/]*[@-~]\")\n\n\ndef require(condition, message):\n    if not condition:\n        raise ValueError(message)\n\n\ndef integer(value, minimum=0):\n    return type(value) is int and value >= minimum\n\n\ndef unique_object(pairs):\n    value = {}\n    for key, item in pairs:\n        require(key not in value, \"Duplicate JSON key\")\n        value[key] = item\n    return value\n\n\ndef decode(raw):\n    return json.loads(raw, object_pairs_hook=unique_object)\n\n\ndef unit_summary(raw):\n    text = ANSI.sub(\"\", raw)\n    result = {}\n    for label, key in ((\"Test Files\", \"files\"), (\"Tests\", \"tests\")):\n        lines = re.findall(r\"(?m)^\\s*\" + label + r\"\\s+([^\\n]+)$\", text)\n        require(len(lines) == 1, \"Missing or multiple Vitest \" + label + \" summaries\")\n        match = re.fullmatch(r\"(\\d+) passed \\((\\d+)\\)\\s*\", lines[0])\n        require(match is not None, \"Incomplete or unknown Vitest \" + label + \" summary\")\n        passed, collected = map(int, match.groups())\n        require(passed == collected and passed > 0, \"Vitest collection was not entirely successful\")\n        result[key] = collected\n    require(len(re.findall(r\"(?m)^\\s*Duration\\s+\\d\", text)) == 1, \"Missing or multiple Vitest completion lines\")\n    require(not re.search(r\"(?mi)^\\s*(?:Errors\\s+\\d|Unhandled Errors|FAIL\\b|Retry #\\d)|\\(retry #\\d|^\\s*\\d+ (?:failed|skipped|flaky|interrupted|todo|fixme)\\b\", text),\n            \"Vitest error or retry output\")\n    return result\n\n\ndef playwright_summary(raw):\n    text = ANSI.sub(\"\", raw)\n    collected = re.findall(r\"(?m)^Running (\\d+) tests? using \\d+ workers?\\s*$\", text)\n    passed = re.findall(r\"(?m)^\\s*(\\d+) passed \\([^\\n]+\\)\\s*$\", text)\n    require(len(collected) == len(passed) == 1 and collected == passed and int(passed[0]) > 0,\n            \"Incomplete, duplicate or unknown Playwright summary\")\n    require(not re.search(r\"(?mi)^\\s*\\d+ (?:failed|skipped|flaky|interrupted|did not run|expected failures?|todo|fixme)\\b|^\\s*Retry #\\d|\\(retry #\\d\", text),\n            \"Playwright incomplete or retry summary\")\n    return {\"tests\": int(passed[0]), \"allCollectedPassed\": True}\n\n\ndef image_summary(raw, head):\n    text = ANSI.sub(\"\", raw)\n    sizes = re.findall(r\"(?m)^Runtime image verification passed \\((\\d+) bytes\\)\\.$\", text)\n    require(len(sizes) == 1 and 0 < int(sizes[0]) < 1_000_000_000, \"Unknown runtime image size proof\")\n    require(text.count(\"Report Summary\") == 1, \"Unknown or duplicate Trivy report\")\n    table = text.split(\"Report Summary\", 1)[1]\n    require(\"Legend:\" in table, \"Truncated Trivy report\")\n    rows = [line.strip().split(\"│\")[1:-1] for line in table.splitlines() if line.strip().startswith(\"│\")]\n    rows = [[cell.strip() for cell in row] for row in rows]\n    require(rows and rows[0] == [\"Target\", \"Type\", \"Vulnerabilities\", \"Secrets\"], \"Unknown Trivy table schema\")\n    targets = []\n    for row in rows[1:]:\n        require(len(row) == 4, \"Unknown Trivy column count\")\n        if row[1:] == [\"\", \"\", \"\"]:\n            require(bool(targets) and bool(row[0]), \"Orphan Trivy target continuation\")\n            targets[-1][0] += row[0]\n        else:\n            targets.append(row)\n    require(bool(targets), \"Empty Trivy report\")\n    require(all(len(row) == 4 and row[0] and row[1] and row[2:] == [\"0\", \"-\"] for row in targets),\n            \"Unscanned, nonzero or unknown Trivy target\")\n    require(len({row[0] for row in targets}) == len(targets), \"Duplicate Trivy targets\")\n    require(targets[0][0].startswith(\"evorto-local-security:\" + head + \" (\"), \"Trivy image identity mismatch\")\n    result = {\"runtimeBytes\": int(sizes[0]), \"targets\": len(targets), \"highCriticalVulnerabilities\": 0}\n    for key in (\"manifest\", \"config\"):\n        matches = re.findall(r\"(?m)^#\\d+ exporting \" + key + r\" (sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}) done$\", text)\n        require(len(matches) == 1, \"Unknown image export \" + key)\n        result[key] = matches[0]\n    return result\n\n\nclass Verifier:\n    def __init__(self, specification):\n        self.spec = specification\n        self.review = Path(specification[\"reviewRoot\"]).resolve()\n        self.repo = Path(specification[\"gitRepository\"]).resolve()\n        self.head, self.tree = specification[\"head\"], specification[\"tree\"]\n        require(re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-f]{40}\", self.head) and re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-f]{40}\", self.tree), \"Expected full Git identities\")\n        self.files = {}\n        self.results = {}\n\n    def path(self, value, base=None):\n        path = Path(value)\n        if not path.is_absolute():\n            path = (base or self.review) / path\n        require(not path.is_symlink(), \"Evidence file is a symlink\")\n        path = path.resolve()\n        require(path.is_relative_to(self.review) and path.is_file(), \"Evidence file is missing or outside review root\")\n        return path\n\n    def read(self, value, expected=None, base=None):\n        path = self.path(value, base)\n        raw = path.read_bytes()\n        digest = hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()\n        if expected is not None:\n            require(re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-f]{64}\", expected) and digest == expected, \"Evidence hash mismatch: \" + str(path.relative_to(self.review)))\n        self.files[str(path.relative_to(self.review))] = {\"sha256\": digest, \"bytes\": len(raw)}\n        return raw\n\n    def same_binding(self, left, right):\n        return self.path(left[\"path\"]) == self.path(right[\"path\"]) and left[\"sha256\"] == right[\"sha256\"]\n\n    def document(self, descriptor):\n        return decode(self.read(descriptor[\"path\"], descriptor[\"sha256\"]))\n\n    def git(self, *args):\n        # Read committed objects only. Do not query or mutate the active checkout.\n        result = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"--no-optional-locks\", \"-C\", str(self.repo), *args],\n                                capture_output=True, timeout=30)\n        require(result.returncode == 0, \"Read-only Git object lookup failed\")\n        return result.stdout\n\n    def identity(self, value, clean=False):\n        require(value[\"head\"] == self.head and value[\"tree\"] == self.tree, \"Recorded head/tree mismatch\")\n        if clean:\n            require(value[\"status\"] == \"\", \"Recorded source is not clean\")\n\n    def envelope(self, receipt, invocation=None):\n        self.identity(receipt)\n        for key in (\"sourceBefore\", \"sourceAfter\"):\n            self.identity(receipt[key], clean=True)\n        require(receipt[\"errors\"] == [], \"Receipt records errors\")\n        require(receipt[\"tools\"] == TOOLS, \"Tool version mismatch\")\n        require(bool(receipt[\"slotGrant\"]) and receipt[\"slotGrant\"] != \"ACTUAL_ROOT_GRANT_REQUIRED\", \"Missing actual grant record\")\n        if invocation:\n            self.identity(invocation)\n            require(receipt[\"parent\"] == invocation[\"parent\"], \"Parent identity mismatch\")\n            require(self.git(\"rev-parse\", self.head + \"^\").decode().strip() == invocation[\"parent\"], \"Commit parent mismatch\")\n\n    def scripts(self, scripts, hashes=None):\n        package = decode(self.git(\"show\", self.head + \":package.json\"))\n        require(all(package[\"scripts\"][name] == command for name, command in scripts.items()), \"Canonical package script mismatch\")\n        for path, digest in (hashes or {}).items():\n            require(hashlib.sha256(self.git(\"show\", self.head + \":\" + path)).hexdigest() == digest,\n                    \"Bound canonical source hash mismatch: \" + path)\n\n    def probes(self, diagnostics):\n        require(isinstance(diagnostics, list), \"Unknown group-probe diagnostics\")\n        for probe in diagnostics:\n            require(probe[\"errno\"] == 1 and integer(probe[\"censusExitCode\"]) and probe[\"censusExitCode\"] == 0\n                    and type(probe[\"leaderExitCode\"]) is int and probe[\"remainingMemberPids\"] == []\n                    and probe[\"absenceConfirmedByNativeCensus\"] is True, \"Unresolved process-group probe\")\n\n    def command(self, item, expected, directory, bound):\n        require(item[\"command\"] == expected, \"Invocation/recorded command mismatch\")\n        require(item[\"status\"] == \"passed\" and type(item[\"exitCode\"]) is int and item[\"exitCode\"] == 0,\n                \"Command did not pass\")\n        require(not any(key in item for key in (\"error\", \"termination\", \"retry\", \"retries\")), \"Command termination/retry evidence\")\n        require(integer(item[\"pid\"], 1) and item[\"pgid\"] == item[\"pid\"] and item[\"processGroupAbsent\"] is True,\n                \"Command process-group cleanup not proven\")\n        self.probes(item.get(\"groupProbeDiagnostics\", []))\n        require(type(item[\"seconds\"]) in (int, float) and 0 <= item[\"seconds\"] <= bound, \"Command exceeded declared bound\")\n        raw = self.read(item[\"log\"], item[\"sha256\"], directory)\n        require(len(raw) == item[\"bytes\"], \"Raw log byte-count mismatch\")\n        return raw.decode(\"utf8\")\n\n    def retained(self, record):\n        for path, digest in record.get(\"retainedLogHashes\", {}).items():\n            self.read(path, digest)\n\n    def source(self):\n        cfg = self.spec[\"source\"]\n        inv, rec = self.document(cfg[\"invocation\"]), self.document(cfg[\"receipt\"])\n        self.envelope(rec, inv)\n        require(rec[\"status\"] in (\n            \"source-gates-passed; root PG and image acceptance pending\",\n            \"source-gates-passed; fresh root PG required before image/runtime preparation\"), \"Source receipt is not successful\")\n        require(rec[\"invocationSha256\"] == cfg[\"invocation\"][\"sha256\"], \"Source invocation binding mismatch\")\n        self.read(inv[\"sourceCommand\"][1], rec[\"runnerSha256\"])\n        require(rec[\"helperSha256\"] == OWNERSHIP_SHA, \"Unreviewed source ownership helper\")\n        self.read(cfg[\"ownershipHelper\"], OWNERSHIP_SHA)\n        require(inv[\"requiredVersions\"] == TOOLS, \"Invocation tools mismatch\")\n        self.scripts(inv[\"canonicalSourceScripts\"], inv.get(\"sourceScriptFileHashes\"))\n        for artifact in inv.get(\"boundExternalArtifacts\", []):\n            self.read(artifact[\"path\"], artifact[\"sha256\"])\n        steps = inv[\"commands\"]\n        require([step[\"name\"] for step in steps] == list(rec[\"commands\"]), \"Missing, repeated or reordered source command\")\n        require(set(SOURCE_COMMANDS) <= set(rec[\"commands\"]), \"Missing required source gate\")\n        results = {}\n        directory = self.path(cfg[\"receipt\"][\"path\"]).parent\n        for step in steps:\n            name, command = step[\"name\"], step[\"command\"]\n            require(name in SOURCE_COMMANDS or name in (\"types\", \"tooling-lint\"), \"Unreviewed additional source gate\")\n            if name in SOURCE_COMMANDS:\n                require(command == SOURCE_COMMANDS[name], \"Noncanonical source command\")\n            raw = self.command(rec[\"commands\"][name], command, directory, inv[\"processTimeoutSeconds\"])\n            if name in (\"server\", \"app\"):\n                results[name] = unit_summary(raw)\n            elif name == \"clean-diff\":\n                require(raw == \"\", \"Clean diff contains output\")\n            elif name == \"format\":\n                require(\"All matched files use Prettier code style!\" in raw, \"Unknown format success output\")\n            elif name in (\"types\", \"tooling-lint\"):\n                self.extra_source(name, raw, command, inv, directory, results)\n        if \"evidence\" in cfg:\n            evidence = self.document(cfg[\"evidence\"])\n            self.identity(evidence)\n            require(evidence[\"sourceBefore\"] == rec[\"sourceBefore\"] and evidence[\"sourceAfter\"] == rec[\"sourceAfter\"]\n                    and evidence[\"tools\"] == rec[\"tools\"] and evidence[\"sourceRunnerReceiptSha256\"] == cfg[\"receipt\"][\"sha256\"], \"Source review binding mismatch\")\n            require(set(evidence[\"gates\"]) == set(rec[\"commands\"]), \"Source review gate set mismatch\")\n            for name, gate in evidence[\"gates\"].items():\n                command = rec[\"commands\"][name]\n                require(gate[\"passed\"] is True and gate[\"command\"] == command[\"command\"] and gate[\"sha256\"] == command[\"sha256\"], \"Source review gate mismatch\")\n                self.read(gate[\"log\"], gate[\"sha256\"])\n                if name in (\"server\", \"app\"):\n                    require(all(gate[k] == v for k, v in results[name].items()) and gate[\"allCollectedPassed\"] is True and gate[\"incompleteSummaries\"] == [], \"Source review summary mismatch\")\n            self.retained(evidence)\n        self.results[\"source\"] = results\n        return inv\n\n    def extra_source(self, name, raw, command, inv, directory, results):\n        require(command[0] == \"node\" and len(command) == 2, \"Unknown supplemental command shape\")\n        descriptor = inv[\"strictGraph\" if name == \"types\" else \"supplementalToolingLint\"]\n        probe = descriptor[\"preparedProbe\"]\n        require(command[1] == probe[\"path\"], \"Supplemental probe mismatch\")\n        self.read(probe[\"path\"], probe[\"sha256\"])\n        value = decode(raw.strip())\n        if name == \"types\":\n            require(value[\"diagnostics\"] == 0 and value[\"strict\"] is True and integer(value[\"roots\"], 1)\n                    and integer(value[\"firstPartySources\"], value[\"roots\"]), \"Strict summary is not successful\")\n            roots = decode(self.read(directory / \"roots.json\"))\n            expected = decode(self.read(descriptor[\"expectedRootSet\"][\"path\"], descriptor[\"expectedRootSet\"][\"sha256\"]))\n            require(roots == expected == descriptor[\"rootNames\"] and len(roots) == value[\"roots\"] == descriptor[\"expectedRootCount\"], \"Actual strict roots differ from invocation\")\n            require(value[\"skipLibCheck\"] == descriptor[\"compilerConfiguration\"][\"inheritedSkipLibCheck\"], \"Strict compiler options mismatch\")\n            require(decode(self.read(directory / \"diagnostics.json\")) == [], \"Strict diagnostics artifact is nonempty\")\n            results[name] = value\n        else:\n            require(isinstance(value, list) and len(value) == len(descriptor[\"rootNames\"]), \"Unknown tooling summary\")\n            require({str(Path(item[\"filePath\"]).relative_to(inv[\"proofCheckout\"])) for item in value} == set(descriptor[\"rootNames\"]), \"Tooling root set mismatch\")\n            require(all(all(item[key] == 0 for key in (\"errorCount\", \"warningCount\", \"fatalErrorCount\")) for item in value), \"Tooling warnings/errors present\")\n            results[name] = {\"files\": len(value), \"errors\": 0, \"warnings\": 0}\n\n    def postgres(self, descriptor, cleanup_descriptor):\n        rec, cleanup = self.document(descriptor), self.document(cleanup_descriptor)\n        self.identity(rec)\n        for key in (\"sourceBefore\", \"sourceAfter\"):\n            self.identity(rec[key], clean=True)\n        require(rec[\"status\"] == \"passed\" and rec[\"exitCode\"] == 0 and rec[\"command\"] == [\"bun\", \"run\", \"test:integration:postgres\"], \"PostgreSQL gate failed or selected\")\n        result = unit_summary(self.read(rec[\"log\"], rec[\"sha256\"]).decode())\n        require(cleanup[\"containerId\"] == rec[\"databaseContainerId\"], \"PostgreSQL cleanup owner mismatch\")\n        counts = cleanup[\"readback\"]\n        require(set(counts) >= {\"urlRaceTenants\", \"concurrencyTenants\", \"idleInTransaction\", \"activeClientQueries\"}\n                and all(type(value) is int and value == 0 for value in counts.values()), \"PostgreSQL cleanup readback is not zero\")\n        result[\"cleanupReadback\"] = counts\n        result[\"processGroupEvidence\"] = \"Not recorded by this standalone PostgreSQL receipt; not independently certified\"\n        self.results[\"postgres\"] = result\n\n    def image(self):\n        cfg = self.spec[\"image\"]\n        inv, rec = self.document(cfg[\"invocation\"]), self.document(cfg[\"receipt\"])\n        self.envelope(rec, inv)\n        require(rec[\"status\"] == \"passed\" and rec[\"invocationSha256\"] == cfg[\"invocation\"][\"sha256\"], \"Image receipt/invocation failed\")\n        self.read(cfg[\"runner\"], rec[\"runnerSha256\"])\n        require(rec[\"ownershipHelperSha256\"] == OWNERSHIP_SHA, \"Unreviewed image ownership helper\")\n        self.read(cfg[\"ownershipHelper\"], OWNERSHIP_SHA)\n        for key in (\"sourceEvidence\", \"postgresEvidence\", \"postgresCleanup\"):\n            self.document(inv[key])\n        require(self.same_binding(inv[\"sourceEvidence\"], self.spec[\"source\"][\"evidence\"]), \"Image/source evidence binding mismatch\")\n        self.postgres(inv[\"postgresEvidence\"], inv[\"postgresCleanup\"])\n        self.scripts({\"image:security:local\": inv[\"script\"]}, inv[\"canonicalSourceHashes\"])\n        require(all(inv[\"canonicalSourceHashes\"].get(key) == digest for key, digest in IMAGE_CHECKS.items()), \"Image silent-check script needs fresh review\")\n        require(inv[\"command\"] == [\"bun\", \"run\", \"image:security:local\"] and list(rec[\"commands\"]) == [\"image\"], \"Image retry/recovery/noncanonical command\")\n        require(inv[\"image\"] == \"evorto-local-security:\" + self.head, \"Image tag identity mismatch\")\n        require(rec[\"environment\"] == inv[\"environment\"], \"Image environment mismatch\")\n        require(all(inv[\"environment\"].get(key) == value for key, value in {\"CI\": \"true\", \"TRIVY_IGNORE_UNFIXED\": \"false\", \"TRIVY_SKIP_DB_UPDATE\": \"false\"}.items()), \"Image scan is not strict\")\n        for state in (rec[\"imageBefore\"], rec[\"cleanup\"][\"imageAfter\"]):\n            require(state[\"exists\"] is False and integer(state[\"exitCode\"], 1), \"Exact image absence was not proven\")\n        require(rec[\"cleanup\"][\"ownedCommandStarted\"] is True and \"afterRecovery\" not in rec[\"cleanup\"], \"Image cleanup required recovery\")\n        require(all(row[\"status\"] != \"Running\" for row in rec[\"buildHistoryBefore\"]), \"Image started alongside another build\")\n        require(rec[\"buildHistoryAfter\"] and all(row[\"status\"] == \"Completed\" and row[\"completed_steps\"] == row[\"total_steps\"] for row in rec[\"buildHistoryAfter\"]), \"Image build did not fully complete\")\n        raw = self.command(rec[\"commands\"][\"image\"], inv[\"command\"], self.path(cfg[\"receipt\"][\"path\"]).parent, inv[\"wholeCommandTimeoutSeconds\"])\n        result = image_summary(raw, self.head)\n        result.update(includeUnfixed=True, databaseUpdatesEnabled=True,\n                      sourceMapsAndSbom=\"Silent nonempty checks bound to reviewed canonical script and successful command; temporary files not re-read\")\n        review = self.document(cfg[\"review\"])\n        self.identity(review)\n        require(review[\"passed\"] is True and review[\"receiptSha256\"] == cfg[\"receipt\"][\"sha256\"] and review[\"logSha256\"] == rec[\"commands\"][\"image\"][\"sha256\"], \"Image review binding mismatch\")\n        require(all(review[key] == result[key] for key in (\"runtimeBytes\", \"manifest\", \"config\", \"targets\", \"highCriticalVulnerabilities\", \"includeUnfixed\", \"databaseUpdatesEnabled\")), \"Image review/raw summary mismatch\")\n        require(review[\"sourceCleanBeforeAfter\"] is True and review[\"ownedImageAndGroupAbsent\"] is True, \"Image review cleanup incomplete\")\n        self.results[\"image\"] = result\n\n    def combined(self):\n        descriptor = self.spec[\"combined\"]\n        rec = self.document(descriptor)\n        self.identity(rec)\n        require(rec[\"tools\"] == TOOLS and rec[\"sourceCleanBeforeAfter\"] is True, \"Combined source identity/tool mismatch\")\n        for item in rec[\"evidence\"].values():\n            self.document(item)\n        self.retained(rec)\n        require(self.same_binding(rec[\"evidence\"][\"sourceRunner\"], self.spec[\"source\"][\"receipt\"])\n                and self.same_binding(rec[\"evidence\"][\"source\"], self.spec[\"source\"][\"evidence\"])\n                and self.same_binding(rec[\"evidence\"][\"imageRunner\"], self.spec[\"image\"][\"receipt\"])\n                and self.same_binding(rec[\"evidence\"][\"image\"], self.spec[\"image\"][\"review\"]), \"Combined evidence identity mismatch\")\n        require(set(rec[\"gates\"]) == set(self.document(self.spec[\"source\"][\"receipt\"])[\"commands\"]) | {\"postgres\", \"image\"}, \"Combined gate set mismatch\")\n        for gate in rec[\"gates\"].values():\n            require(gate[\"passed\"] is True, \"Combined gate is not passed\")\n        evidence = self.document(self.spec[\"source\"][\"evidence\"])\n        require(all(rec[\"gates\"][name] == gate for name, gate in evidence[\"gates\"].items()), \"Combined source gates differ from source evidence\")\n        for name in (\"server\", \"app\"):\n            require(all(rec[\"gates\"][name][key] == value for key, value in self.results[\"source\"][name].items()), \"Combined unit summary mismatch\")\n        pg = rec[\"gates\"][\"postgres\"]\n        require(all(pg[key] == self.results[\"postgres\"][key] for key in (\"files\", \"tests\", \"cleanupReadback\")) and pg[\"allCollectedPassed\"] is True, \"Combined PostgreSQL summary mismatch\")\n        image_review = self.document(self.spec[\"image\"][\"review\"])\n        require(all(key in image_review and value == image_review[key] for key, value in rec[\"gates\"][\"image\"].items()), \"Combined image summary differs from image review\")\n        require(self.same_binding(rec[\"evidence\"][\"postgres\"], self.document(self.spec[\"image\"][\"invocation\"])[\"postgresEvidence\"])\n                and self.same_binding(rec[\"evidence\"][\"postgresCleanup\"], self.document(self.spec[\"image\"][\"invocation\"])[\"postgresCleanup\"]), \"Combined PostgreSQL binding mismatch\")\n\n    def runtime(self):\n        cfg = self.spec[\"runtime\"]\n        rec, plan = self.document(cfg[\"receipt\"]), self.document(cfg[\"plan\"])\n        self.identity(rec)\n        require(rec[\"status\"] == \"passed\" and rec[\"errors\"] == [] and rec[\"runnerSha256\"] == RUNTIME_V2_SHA,\n                \"Only successful normal v2 runtime receipts are supported; failed00 requires separate review\")\n        self.read(cfg[\"runner\"], RUNTIME_V2_SHA)\n        require(rec[\"planSha256\"] == cfg[\"plan\"][\"sha256\"] and plan[\"runnerSha256\"] == RUNTIME_V2_SHA, \"Runtime plan binding mismatch\")\n        self.document(plan[\"inventory\"])\n        require(rec[\"inventorySha256\"] == plan[\"inventory\"][\"sha256\"], \"Runtime inventory binding mismatch\")\n        entries = [row for row in plan[\"entries\"] if row[\"head\"] == self.head]\n        require(len(entries) == 1, \"Runtime target is not uniquely admitted\")\n        entry = entries[0]\n        self.identity(entry)\n        require(isinstance(entry[\"layerLabel\"], str) and re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9]{2}[a-z]?\", entry[\"layerLabel\"]), \"Missing or invalid layer label\")\n        require(re.fullmatch(re.escape(\"evorto-prefix-\" + entry[\"layerLabel\"] + \"-\" + self.head[:8] + \"-\") + r\"[a-z0-9]{1,8}\", rec[\"project\"]), \"Runtime project/layer identity mismatch\")\n        require(entry[\"ordinaryReceipt\"] == self.spec[\"combined\"][\"path\"] and entry[\"receiptSha256\"] == self.spec[\"combined\"][\"sha256\"], \"Runtime ordinary prerequisite mismatch\")\n        approval = self.document({\"path\": entry[\"readinessApproval\"], \"sha256\": entry[\"readinessApprovalSha256\"]})\n        self.identity(approval)\n        require(approval[\"status\"] == \"approved\" and approval[\"ordinaryReceiptSha256\"] == self.spec[\"combined\"][\"sha256\"]\n                and approval[\"runnerSha256\"] == RUNTIME_V2_SHA and approval[\"slotGrant\"] == rec[\"slotGrant\"], \"Runtime readiness approval mismatch\")\n        require(rec[\"ordinaryReceiptCountValidated\"] == len(plan[\"entries\"]) and rec[\"registeredPrefixCountValidated\"] == len(plan[\"registeredPrefixes\"])\n                and rec[\"historicalReceiptCountValidated\"] == len(plan[\"historicalOrdinaryEntries\"]), \"Runtime plan validation counts mismatch\")\n        require(plan[\"commands\"] == RUNTIME_COMMANDS and plan[\"noAutomaticRetry\"] is True, \"Runtime canonical command policy mismatch\")\n        require(plan[\"nodeVersion\"] == TOOLS[\"node\"] and plan[\"bunVersion\"] == TOOLS[\"bun\"], \"Runtime pinned tools mismatch\")\n        self.scripts(entry[\"canonicalScripts\"])\n        for key in (\"sourceSelected\", \"sourceAfter\"):\n            self.identity(rec[key], clean=True)\n        require(rec[\"sourceBeforeSelection\"][\"status\"] == \"\", \"Runtime started from dirty source\")\n        require(rec[\"trackedFileReadability\"] == {\"unreadableCount\": 0, \"paths\": []}, \"Runtime source readability failed\")\n        expected = {\"checkout\": [\"git\", \"switch\", \"--detach\", self.head], **{k:v for k,v in RUNTIME_COMMANDS.items() if k != \"runtime\"}}\n        require(list(rec[\"commands\"]) == list(expected), \"Runtime has missing/repeated/recovery commands\")\n        results = {}\n        directory = self.path(cfg[\"receipt\"][\"path\"]).parent\n        for name, command in expected.items():\n            item = rec[\"commands\"][name]\n            raw = self.command(item, command, directory, 1200 if name in (\"functional\", \"documentation\") else 300)\n            if name in (\"functional\", \"documentation\"):\n                result = playwright_summary(raw)\n                require(item[\"collected\"] == item[\"passed\"] == [result[\"tests\"]] and item[\"incompleteSummaryCount\"] == 0 and item[\"allCollectedPassed\"] is True, \"Runtime/raw summary mismatch\")\n                results[name] = result\n        runtime = rec[\"runtime\"]\n        require(runtime[\"command\"] == RUNTIME_COMMANDS[\"runtime\"] and runtime[\"pgid\"] == runtime[\"pid\"], \"Runtime supervisor identity mismatch\")\n        raw = self.read(runtime[\"log\"], runtime[\"sha256\"], directory)\n        require(len(raw) == runtime[\"bytes\"], \"Runtime raw log size mismatch\")\n        identity = runtime[\"identity\"]\n        self.identity(identity)\n        require(identity[\"readinessStatus\"] == 204 and identity[\"project\"] == rec[\"project\"]\n                and identity[\"workingDirectory\"] == plan[\"proofCheckout\"] and rec[\"ports\"] == entry[\"ports\"], \"Runtime project/checkout/readiness mismatch\")\n        require(re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-f]{64}\", identity[\"containerId\"]) and re.fullmatch(r\"sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}\", identity[\"imageId\"]), \"Invalid container/image identity\")\n        cleanup = rec[\"cleanup\"]\n        empty = {\"containers\": [], \"networks\": [], \"volumes\": []}\n        require(cleanup[\"errors\"] == [] and cleanup[\"remainingResources\"] == empty and cleanup[\"portsReleased\"] is True\n                and \"afterRecoveryResources\" not in cleanup, \"Runtime cleanup failed or required recovery\")\n        supervisor = cleanup[\"supervisor\"]\n        require(supervisor[\"exitCode\"] in (0, -15, 143) and supervisor[\"signals\"] in ([], [\"SIGTERM\"])\n                and supervisor[\"wasAlreadyExited\"] is False and supervisor[\"processGroupAbsent\"] is True, \"Runtime supervisor shutdown was not normal\")\n        self.probes(supervisor[\"groupProbeDiagnostics\"])\n        self.probes(cleanup[\"groupProbeDiagnostics\"])\n        if \"review\" in cfg:\n            review = self.document(cfg[\"review\"])\n            self.identity(review)\n            require(review[\"receiptSha256\"] == cfg[\"receipt\"][\"sha256\"] and review[\"ordinaryReceiptSha256\"] == self.spec[\"combined\"][\"sha256\"], \"Runtime review binding mismatch\")\n            require(review[\"functionalTests\"] == results[\"functional\"][\"tests\"] and review[\"documentationTests\"] == results[\"documentation\"][\"tests\"] and review[\"allCollectedPassed\"] is True and review[\"noRetries\"] is True, \"Runtime review summaries mismatch\")\n            require(review[\"cleanup\"] == cleanup and review[\"runtimeIdentity\"] == identity and review[\"cleanSourceBeforeAfter\"] is True\n                    and review[\"currentResources\"] == empty and review[\"currentPortsClosed\"] is True, \"Runtime review cleanup mismatch\")\n            require(set(review[\"currentOwnedProcessGroupsAbsent\"]) == {runtime[\"pgid\"], *(item[\"pgid\"] for item in rec[\"commands\"].values())}, \"Runtime reviewed process groups mismatch\")\n        self.results[\"runtime\"] = results\n\n    def verify(self):\n        require(self.git(\"rev-parse\", self.head + \"^{tree}\").decode().strip() == self.tree, \"Committed head/tree mismatch\")\n        self.source()\n        if \"image\" in self.spec:\n            self.image()\n        if \"combined\" in self.spec:\n            require(\"image\" in self.spec, \"Combined proof requires image inputs\")\n            self.combined()\n        if \"runtime\" in self.spec:\n            require(\"combined\" in self.spec, \"Runtime proof requires combined ordinary proof\")\n            self.runtime()\n        return self.results\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--input\", required=True, type=Path)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--output\", required=True, type=Path)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    require(not args.output.exists(), \"Refusing to replace an existing result\")\n    spec_raw = args.input.read_bytes()\n    verifier = None\n    result = {\"status\": \"failed\", \"inputSha256\": hashlib.sha256(spec_raw).hexdigest(),\n              \"verifierSha256\": hashlib.sha256(Path(__file__).read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n              \"checkedAt\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n              \"scope\": \"Offline evidence consistency only; no gate execution, current liveness proof, or approval\"}\n    try:\n        verifier = Verifier(decode(spec_raw))\n        result.update(head=verifier.head, tree=verifier.tree, gates=verifier.verify(), status=\"verified\")\n    except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError, OSError, UnicodeError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as error:\n        result[\"error\"] = {\"type\": type(error).__name__, \"reason\": str(error)}\n    if verifier:\n        result[\"verifiedFiles\"] = verifier.files\n    args.output.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    with args.output.open(\"x\") as handle:\n        json.dump(result, handle, indent=2)\n        handle.write(\"\\n\")\n    args.output.chmod(0o600)\n    print(json.dumps({\"status\": result[\"status\"], \"output\": str(args.output)}))\n    return 0 if result[\"status\"] == \"verified\" else 1\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# Prefix result verifier proposal\n\n`verify_results.py` verifies saved successful source, image and normal v2 runtime receipts. It does not execute gates, approve a prefix, inspect current processes/services, change refs, or repair evidence. Root review is required before operational use.\n\nRun with an explicit input manifest and a **new** output filename:\n\n```sh\npython3 prefix-runtime-verification/result-verifier-proposal/verify_results.py \\\n  --input prefix-runtime-verification/result-verifier-proposal/inputs/successful-01-v2.json \\\n  --output /absolute/path/to/a/new/result.json\n```\n\nThe output is `verified` with exit 0 only if every requested stage passes. Unknown formats, missing bindings, failed receipts, mismatched hashes and unsupported commands fail with exit 1. Existing output files are never replaced. Only read-only `git rev-parse` and `git show` subprocesses are used; the active checkout can belong to another prefix.\n\n## Input and checks\n\nThe example manifest supplies `reviewRoot`, `gitRepository`, full `head`/`tree`, and explicit `{path, sha256}` descriptors. `source` is required; `image`, `combined` and `runtime` may be added as their actual evidence becomes available. Image requires its source-evidence descriptor; combined requires image; runtime requires combined. Relative paths resolve within the review artifact root. Rebind the manifest to each exact prefix; never relabel a historical result.\n\n- **Source:** committed head/tree/parent; clean recorded before/after identities; pinned Node 24.15.0/Bun 1.3.14; invocation, runner and reviewed ownership-helper hashes; exact ordered invocation commands with no missing/extra gates; zero exits and absent command groups; raw-log hash/size; canonical package scripts and declared source/probe hashes. Both full Vitest summaries must occur once with positive equal passed/collected counts and no incomplete/retry/error summary. The actual layer 15 `types` and `tooling-lint` commands are supported through its declared probes, strict root set/options and diagnostic artifacts. Unknown extra command names fail.\n- **Image:** successful canonical command, exact revision tag, strict unfixed/update flags, clean source, positive tag absence before/after, completed builds and absent process group. The raw runtime-size line and complete wrapped Trivy table are parsed; every target must report zero findings. Exported manifest/config and all parsed values must match the root review and combined evidence. Two reviewed image-check script hashes are pinned because their source-map and SPDX nonempty checks are silent. If either script changes, obtain a source review and update the allowlist deliberately.\n- **PostgreSQL prerequisite:** exact identity, full unselected canonical command with exit 0, complete raw Vitest counts, same cleanup container, and all recorded scoped cleanup counters zero. The existing standalone PG receipt does not record a process group; the result explicitly leaves that proof uncertified.\n- **Runtime:** only `status: passed` from the reviewed v2 runner; exact immutable plan snapshot, inventory, admitted `layerLabel`/canonical scripts, readiness approval and combined prerequisite; exact checkout/install/full functional/full docs sequence; each raw-log hash/size and complete Playwright summary; runtime project/checkout/container/image/readiness identities; normal supervisor exit, group absence, empty resources and released ports. Failed layer 00 plus its exceptional cleanup supplement is deliberately unsupported. Preparation failures before execution do not become test retries; acceptance still requires the later actual successful receipt and exact accepted plan.\n\nAll bound raw logs in this prefix's supplied receipt chain are rehashed, including PostgreSQL and runtime-supervisor logs. The helper does not repeat the separate historical inventory audit across other prefixes. Recorded cleanup and source snapshots are evidence of the original run, not a fresh live-state census. It does not claim exported temporary archives still exist after canonical cleanup.\n\n## Offline comparison\n\n`dry-run-01/final.json` verifies the unchanged successful 01 records: **33 evidence files / 15 raw logs**, server **168 files / 1,351 tests**, app **111 / 802**, PG **14 / 55**, functional **151**, docs **52**, runtime image **95,708,630 bytes**, **297 targets / 0 HIGH or CRITICAL findings**. No application/provider/DB/runtime/compile command was run.\n\n`compare_offline.py` uses the real 01 logs and in-memory alterations. Its 17 rejection cases cover partial/duplicate/mismatched summaries, retry/flaky output, unknown/unscanned Trivy output, wrong identity, dirty source, changed hash, nonzero exit, live groups, unresolved EPERM and a failed runtime with otherwise green tests. The original evidence is never edited. The supplemental layer 15 parsers are source-adapted to its current invocation; fresh layer 15 outputs are still pending and are not claimed verified here.\n\nEarlier dry-run outputs remain: attempt 1 rejected a wrapped Trivy row until the exact continuation format was supported; attempt 2 rejected a newly changed live runtime plan. The corrected input uses root's immutable `plan-replayed-v2-before02.json`, whose hash exactly matches the 01 execution receipt. Attempts 3/4 and final passed. These are verifier development runs, never application test retries.\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Offline receipt verifier. Reads evidence/Git objects; never runs a gate or repairs evidence.\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\n\nTOOLS = {\"node\": \"v24.15.0\", \"bun\": \"1.3.14\"}\nOWNERSHIP_SHA = \"820f0fdd78f77d8cd3dc98586d661b58c1b86d10847c9b2b3d07d1f4253b2215\"\nRUNTIME_V2_SHA = \"b12d86b81a1e66ad8b3777deb5c62a74a8606ec39d925b66a6ab41ab5c3f65c2\"\n# Changes to these two silent-check scripts need a new source review, not substring guesses.\nIMAGE_CHECKS = {\n    \"ops/scaleway/verify-image-security.sh\": \"f56ca53d08227eb0623f2b32954aadc39ccdb09cbb16627a27682c23a0eb1df9\",\n    \"ops/scaleway/verify-runtime-image.sh\": \"d2e887a8481baaa9e787eb443ff23cc3f0550fe1e905ff1e6faae82c5770f972\",\n}\nSOURCE_COMMANDS = {\n    \"install\": [\"bun\", \"install\", \"--frozen-lockfile\"],\n    \"release\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"release:validate\"],\n    \"format\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"format:check\"],\n    \"lint\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"lint\"],\n    \"clean-diff\": [\"git\", \"diff\", \"--exit-code\"],\n    \"server\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"test:unit:server\"],\n    \"app\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"test:unit\"],\n    \"infra\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"infra:check\"],\n}\nRUNTIME_COMMANDS = {\n    \"install\": SOURCE_COMMANDS[\"install\"],\n    \"runtime\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"docker:webserver\"],\n    \"functional\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"test:e2e\"],\n    \"documentation\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"test:e2e:docs\"],\n}\nANSI = re.compile(r\"\\x1b\\[[0-?]*[ -/]*[@-~]\")\n\n\ndef require(condition, message):\n    if not condition:\n        raise ValueError(message)\n\n\ndef integer(value, minimum=0):\n    return type(value) is int and value >= minimum\n\n\ndef unique_object(pairs):\n    value = {}\n    for key, item in pairs:\n        require(key not in value, \"Duplicate JSON key\")\n        value[key] = item\n    return value\n\n\ndef decode(raw):\n    return json.loads(raw, object_pairs_hook=unique_object)\n\n\ndef unit_summary(raw):\n    text = ANSI.sub(\"\", raw)\n    result = {}\n    for label, key in ((\"Test Files\", \"files\"), (\"Tests\", \"tests\")):\n        lines = re.findall(r\"(?m)^\\s*\" + label + r\"\\s+([^\\n]+)$\", text)\n        require(len(lines) == 1, \"Missing or multiple Vitest \" + label + \" summaries\")\n        match = re.fullmatch(r\"(\\d+) passed \\((\\d+)\\)\\s*\", lines[0])\n        require(match is not None, \"Incomplete or unknown Vitest \" + label + \" summary\")\n        passed, collected = map(int, match.groups())\n        require(passed == collected and passed > 0, \"Vitest collection was not entirely successful\")\n        result[key] = collected\n    require(len(re.findall(r\"(?m)^\\s*Duration\\s+\\d\", text)) == 1, \"Missing or multiple Vitest completion lines\")\n    require(not re.search(r\"(?mi)^\\s*(?:Errors\\s+\\d|Unhandled Errors|FAIL\\b|Retry #\\d)|\\(retry #\\d|^\\s*\\d+ (?:failed|skipped|flaky|interrupted|todo|fixme)\\b\", text),\n            \"Vitest error or retry output\")\n    return result\n\n\ndef playwright_summary(raw):\n    text = ANSI.sub(\"\", raw)\n    collected = re.findall(r\"(?m)^Running (\\d+) tests? using \\d+ workers?\\s*$\", text)\n    passed = re.findall(r\"(?m)^\\s*(\\d+) passed \\([^\\n]+\\)\\s*$\", text)\n    require(len(collected) == len(passed) == 1 and collected == passed and int(passed[0]) > 0,\n            \"Incomplete, duplicate or unknown Playwright summary\")\n    require(not re.search(r\"(?mi)^\\s*\\d+ (?:failed|skipped|flaky|interrupted|did not run|expected failures?|todo|fixme)\\b|^\\s*Retry #\\d|\\(retry #\\d\", text),\n            \"Playwright incomplete or retry summary\")\n    return {\"tests\": int(passed[0]), \"allCollectedPassed\": True}\n\n\ndef image_summary(raw, head):\n    text = ANSI.sub(\"\", raw)\n    sizes = re.findall(r\"(?m)^Runtime image verification passed \\((\\d+) bytes\\)\\.$\", text)\n    require(len(sizes) == 1 and 0 < int(sizes[0]) < 1_000_000_000, \"Unknown runtime image size proof\")\n    require(text.count(\"Report Summary\") == 1, \"Unknown or duplicate Trivy report\")\n    table = text.split(\"Report Summary\", 1)[1]\n    require(\"Legend:\" in table, \"Truncated Trivy report\")\n    rows = [line.strip().split(\"│\")[1:-1] for line in table.splitlines() if line.strip().startswith(\"│\")]\n    rows = [[cell.strip() for cell in row] for row in rows]\n    require(rows and rows[0] == [\"Target\", \"Type\", \"Vulnerabilities\", \"Secrets\"], \"Unknown Trivy table schema\")\n    targets = []\n    for row in rows[1:]:\n        require(len(row) == 4, \"Unknown Trivy column count\")\n        if row[1:] == [\"\", \"\", \"\"]:\n            require(bool(targets) and bool(row[0]), \"Orphan Trivy target continuation\")\n            targets[-1][0] += row[0]\n        else:\n            targets.append(row)\n    require(bool(targets), \"Empty Trivy report\")\n    require(all(len(row) == 4 and row[0] and row[1] and row[2:] == [\"0\", \"-\"] for row in targets),\n            \"Unscanned, nonzero or unknown Trivy target\")\n    require(len({row[0] for row in targets}) == len(targets), \"Duplicate Trivy targets\")\n    require(targets[0][0].startswith(\"evorto-local-security:\" + head + \" (\"), \"Trivy image identity mismatch\")\n    result = {\"runtimeBytes\": int(sizes[0]), \"targets\": len(targets), \"highCriticalVulnerabilities\": 0}\n    for key in (\"manifest\", \"config\"):\n        matches = re.findall(r\"(?m)^#\\d+ exporting \" + key + r\" (sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}) done$\", text)\n        require(len(matches) == 1, \"Unknown image export \" + key)\n        result[key] = matches[0]\n    return result\n\n\nclass Verifier:\n    def __init__(self, specification):\n        self.spec = specification\n        self.review = Path(specification[\"reviewRoot\"]).resolve()\n        self.repo = Path(specification[\"gitRepository\"]).resolve()\n        self.head, self.tree = specification[\"head\"], specification[\"tree\"]\n        require(re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-f]{40}\", self.head) and re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-f]{40}\", self.tree), \"Expected full Git identities\")\n        self.files = {}\n        self.results = {}\n\n    def path(self, value, base=None):\n        path = Path(value)\n        if not path.is_absolute():\n            path = (base or self.review) / path\n        require(not path.is_symlink(), \"Evidence file is a symlink\")\n        path = path.resolve()\n        require(path.is_relative_to(self.review) and path.is_file(), \"Evidence file is missing or outside review root\")\n        return path\n\n    def read(self, value, expected=None, base=None):\n        path = self.path(value, base)\n        raw = path.read_bytes()\n        digest = hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()\n        if expected is not None:\n            require(re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-f]{64}\", expected) and digest == expected, \"Evidence hash mismatch: \" + str(path.relative_to(self.review)))\n        self.files[str(path.relative_to(self.review))] = {\"sha256\": digest, \"bytes\": len(raw)}\n        return raw\n\n    def same_binding(self, left, right):\n        return self.path(left[\"path\"]) == self.path(right[\"path\"]) and left[\"sha256\"] == right[\"sha256\"]\n\n    def document(self, descriptor):\n        return decode(self.read(descriptor[\"path\"], descriptor[\"sha256\"]))\n\n    def git(self, *args):\n        # Read committed objects only. Do not query or mutate the active checkout.\n        result = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"--no-optional-locks\", \"-C\", str(self.repo), *args],\n                                capture_output=True, timeout=30)\n        require(result.returncode == 0, \"Read-only Git object lookup failed\")\n        return result.stdout\n\n    def identity(self, value, clean=False):\n        require(value[\"head\"] == self.head and value[\"tree\"] == self.tree, \"Recorded head/tree mismatch\")\n        if clean:\n            require(value[\"status\"] == \"\", \"Recorded source is not clean\")\n\n    def envelope(self, receipt, invocation=None):\n        self.identity(receipt)\n        for key in (\"sourceBefore\", \"sourceAfter\"):\n            self.identity(receipt[key], clean=True)\n        require(receipt[\"errors\"] == [], \"Receipt records errors\")\n        require(receipt[\"tools\"] == TOOLS, \"Tool version mismatch\")\n        require(bool(receipt[\"slotGrant\"]) and receipt[\"slotGrant\"] != \"ACTUAL_ROOT_GRANT_REQUIRED\", \"Missing actual grant record\")\n        if invocation:\n            self.identity(invocation)\n            require(receipt[\"parent\"] == invocation[\"parent\"], \"Parent identity mismatch\")\n            require(self.git(\"rev-parse\", self.head + \"^\").decode().strip() == invocation[\"parent\"], \"Commit parent mismatch\")\n\n    def scripts(self, scripts, hashes=None):\n        package = decode(self.git(\"show\", self.head + \":package.json\"))\n        require(all(package[\"scripts\"][name] == command for name, command in scripts.items()), \"Canonical package script mismatch\")\n        for path, digest in (hashes or {}).items():\n            require(hashlib.sha256(self.git(\"show\", self.head + \":\" + path)).hexdigest() == digest,\n                    \"Bound canonical source hash mismatch: \" + path)\n\n    def probes(self, diagnostics):\n        require(isinstance(diagnostics, list), \"Unknown group-probe diagnostics\")\n        for probe in diagnostics:\n            require(probe[\"errno\"] == 1 and integer(probe[\"censusExitCode\"]) and probe[\"censusExitCode\"] == 0\n                    and type(probe[\"leaderExitCode\"]) is int and probe[\"remainingMemberPids\"] == []\n                    and probe[\"absenceConfirmedByNativeCensus\"] is True, \"Unresolved process-group probe\")\n\n    def command(self, item, expected, directory, bound):\n        require(item[\"command\"] == expected, \"Invocation/recorded command mismatch\")\n        require(item[\"status\"] == \"passed\" and type(item[\"exitCode\"]) is int and item[\"exitCode\"] == 0,\n                \"Command did not pass\")\n        require(not any(key in item for key in (\"error\", \"termination\", \"retry\", \"retries\")), \"Command termination/retry evidence\")\n        require(integer(item[\"pid\"], 1) and item[\"pgid\"] == item[\"pid\"] and item[\"processGroupAbsent\"] is True,\n                \"Command process-group cleanup not proven\")\n        self.probes(item.get(\"groupProbeDiagnostics\", []))\n        require(type(item[\"seconds\"]) in (int, float) and 0 <= item[\"seconds\"] <= bound, \"Command exceeded declared bound\")\n        raw = self.read(item[\"log\"], item[\"sha256\"], directory)\n        require(len(raw) == item[\"bytes\"], \"Raw log byte-count mismatch\")\n        return raw.decode(\"utf8\")\n\n    def retained(self, record):\n        for path, digest in record.get(\"retainedLogHashes\", {}).items():\n            self.read(path, digest)\n\n    def source(self):\n        cfg = self.spec[\"source\"]\n        inv, rec = self.document(cfg[\"invocation\"]), self.document(cfg[\"receipt\"])\n        self.envelope(rec, inv)\n        require(rec[\"status\"] in (\n            \"source-gates-passed; root PG and image acceptance pending\",\n            \"source-gates-passed; fresh root PG required before image/runtime preparation\"), \"Source receipt is not successful\")\n        require(rec[\"invocationSha256\"] == cfg[\"invocation\"][\"sha256\"], \"Source invocation binding mismatch\")\n        self.read(inv[\"sourceCommand\"][1], rec[\"runnerSha256\"])\n        require(rec[\"helperSha256\"] == OWNERSHIP_SHA, \"Unreviewed source ownership helper\")\n        self.read(cfg[\"ownershipHelper\"], OWNERSHIP_SHA)\n        require(inv[\"requiredVersions\"] == TOOLS, \"Invocation tools mismatch\")\n        self.scripts(inv[\"canonicalSourceScripts\"], inv.get(\"sourceScriptFileHashes\"))\n        for artifact in inv.get(\"boundExternalArtifacts\", []):\n            self.read(artifact[\"path\"], artifact[\"sha256\"])\n        steps = inv[\"commands\"]\n        require([step[\"name\"] for step in steps] == list(rec[\"commands\"]), \"Missing, repeated or reordered source command\")\n        require(set(SOURCE_COMMANDS) <= set(rec[\"commands\"]), \"Missing required source gate\")\n        results = {}\n        directory = self.path(cfg[\"receipt\"][\"path\"]).parent\n        for step in steps:\n            name, command = step[\"name\"], step[\"command\"]\n            require(name in SOURCE_COMMANDS or name in (\"types\", \"tooling-lint\"), \"Unreviewed additional source gate\")\n            if name in SOURCE_COMMANDS:\n                require(command == SOURCE_COMMANDS[name], \"Noncanonical source command\")\n            raw = self.command(rec[\"commands\"][name], command, directory, inv[\"processTimeoutSeconds\"])\n            if name in (\"server\", \"app\"):\n                results[name] = unit_summary(raw)\n            elif name == \"clean-diff\":\n                require(raw == \"\", \"Clean diff contains output\")\n            elif name == \"format\":\n                require(\"All matched files use Prettier code style!\" in raw, \"Unknown format success output\")\n            elif name in (\"types\", \"tooling-lint\"):\n                self.extra_source(name, raw, command, inv, directory, results)\n        if \"evidence\" in cfg:\n            evidence = self.document(cfg[\"evidence\"])\n            self.identity(evidence)\n            require(evidence[\"sourceBefore\"] == rec[\"sourceBefore\"] and evidence[\"sourceAfter\"] == rec[\"sourceAfter\"]\n                    and evidence[\"tools\"] == rec[\"tools\"] and evidence[\"sourceRunnerReceiptSha256\"] == cfg[\"receipt\"][\"sha256\"], \"Source review binding mismatch\")\n            require(set(evidence[\"gates\"]) == set(rec[\"commands\"]), \"Source review gate set mismatch\")\n            for name, gate in evidence[\"gates\"].items():\n                command = rec[\"commands\"][name]\n                require(gate[\"passed\"] is True and gate[\"command\"] == command[\"command\"] and gate[\"sha256\"] == command[\"sha256\"], \"Source review gate mismatch\")\n                self.read(gate[\"log\"], gate[\"sha256\"])\n                if name in (\"server\", \"app\"):\n                    require(all(gate[k] == v for k, v in results[name].items()) and gate[\"allCollectedPassed\"] is True and gate[\"incompleteSummaries\"] == [], \"Source review summary mismatch\")\n            self.retained(evidence)\n        self.results[\"source\"] = results\n        return inv\n\n    def extra_source(self, name, raw, command, inv, directory, results):\n        require(command[0] == \"node\" and len(command) == 2, \"Unknown supplemental command shape\")\n        descriptor = inv[\"strictGraph\" if name == \"types\" else \"supplementalToolingLint\"]\n        probe = descriptor[\"preparedProbe\"]\n        require(command[1] == probe[\"path\"], \"Supplemental probe mismatch\")\n        self.read(probe[\"path\"], probe[\"sha256\"])\n        value = decode(raw.strip())\n        if name == \"types\":\n            require(value[\"diagnostics\"] == 0 and value[\"strict\"] is True and integer(value[\"roots\"], 1)\n                    and integer(value[\"firstPartySources\"], value[\"roots\"]), \"Strict summary is not successful\")\n            roots = decode(self.read(directory / \"roots.json\"))\n            expected = decode(self.read(descriptor[\"expectedRootSet\"][\"path\"], descriptor[\"expectedRootSet\"][\"sha256\"]))\n            require(roots == expected == descriptor[\"rootNames\"] and len(roots) == value[\"roots\"] == descriptor[\"expectedRootCount\"], \"Actual strict roots differ from invocation\")\n            require(value[\"skipLibCheck\"] == descriptor[\"compilerConfiguration\"][\"inheritedSkipLibCheck\"], \"Strict compiler options mismatch\")\n            require(decode(self.read(directory / \"diagnostics.json\")) == [], \"Strict diagnostics artifact is nonempty\")\n            results[name] = value\n        else:\n            require(isinstance(value, list) and len(value) == len(descriptor[\"rootNames\"]), \"Unknown tooling summary\")\n            require({str(Path(item[\"filePath\"]).relative_to(inv[\"proofCheckout\"])) for item in value} == set(descriptor[\"rootNames\"]), \"Tooling root set mismatch\")\n            require(all(all(item[key] == 0 for key in (\"errorCount\", \"warningCount\", \"fatalErrorCount\")) for item in value), \"Tooling warnings/errors present\")\n            results[name] = {\"files\": len(value), \"errors\": 0, \"warnings\": 0}\n\n    def postgres(self, descriptor, cleanup_descriptor):\n        rec, cleanup = self.document(descriptor), self.document(cleanup_descriptor)\n        self.identity(rec)\n        for key in (\"sourceBefore\", \"sourceAfter\"):\n            self.identity(rec[key], clean=True)\n        require(rec[\"status\"] == \"passed\" and rec[\"exitCode\"] == 0 and rec[\"command\"] == [\"bun\", \"run\", \"test:integration:postgres\"], \"PostgreSQL gate failed or selected\")\n        result = unit_summary(self.read(rec[\"log\"], rec[\"sha256\"]).decode())\n        require(cleanup[\"containerId\"] == rec[\"databaseContainerId\"], \"PostgreSQL cleanup owner mismatch\")\n        counts = cleanup[\"readback\"]\n        require(set(counts) >= {\"urlRaceTenants\", \"concurrencyTenants\", \"idleInTransaction\", \"activeClientQueries\"}\n                and all(type(value) is int and value == 0 for value in counts.values()), \"PostgreSQL cleanup readback is not zero\")\n        result[\"cleanupReadback\"] = counts\n        result[\"processGroupEvidence\"] = \"Not recorded by this standalone PostgreSQL receipt; not independently certified\"\n        self.results[\"postgres\"] = result\n\n    def image(self):\n        cfg = self.spec[\"image\"]\n        inv, rec = self.document(cfg[\"invocation\"]), self.document(cfg[\"receipt\"])\n        self.envelope(rec, inv)\n        require(rec[\"status\"] == \"passed\" and rec[\"invocationSha256\"] == cfg[\"invocation\"][\"sha256\"], \"Image receipt/invocation failed\")\n        self.read(cfg[\"runner\"], rec[\"runnerSha256\"])\n        require(rec[\"ownershipHelperSha256\"] == OWNERSHIP_SHA, \"Unreviewed image ownership helper\")\n        self.read(cfg[\"ownershipHelper\"], OWNERSHIP_SHA)\n        for key in (\"sourceEvidence\", \"postgresEvidence\", \"postgresCleanup\"):\n            self.document(inv[key])\n        require(self.same_binding(inv[\"sourceEvidence\"], self.spec[\"source\"][\"evidence\"]), \"Image/source evidence binding mismatch\")\n        self.postgres(inv[\"postgresEvidence\"], inv[\"postgresCleanup\"])\n        self.scripts({\"image:security:local\": inv[\"script\"]}, inv[\"canonicalSourceHashes\"])\n        require(all(inv[\"canonicalSourceHashes\"].get(key) == digest for key, digest in IMAGE_CHECKS.items()), \"Image silent-check script needs fresh review\")\n        require(inv[\"command\"] == [\"bun\", \"run\", \"image:security:local\"] and list(rec[\"commands\"]) == [\"image\"], \"Image retry/recovery/noncanonical command\")\n        require(inv[\"image\"] == \"evorto-local-security:\" + self.head, \"Image tag identity mismatch\")\n        require(rec[\"environment\"] == inv[\"environment\"], \"Image environment mismatch\")\n        require(all(inv[\"environment\"].get(key) == value for key, value in {\"CI\": \"true\", \"TRIVY_IGNORE_UNFIXED\": \"false\", \"TRIVY_SKIP_DB_UPDATE\": \"false\"}.items()), \"Image scan is not strict\")\n        for state in (rec[\"imageBefore\"], rec[\"cleanup\"][\"imageAfter\"]):\n            require(state[\"exists\"] is False and integer(state[\"exitCode\"], 1), \"Exact image absence was not proven\")\n        require(rec[\"cleanup\"][\"ownedCommandStarted\"] is True and \"afterRecovery\" not in rec[\"cleanup\"], \"Image cleanup required recovery\")\n        require(all(row[\"status\"] != \"Running\" for row in rec[\"buildHistoryBefore\"]), \"Image started alongside another build\")\n        require(rec[\"buildHistoryAfter\"] and all(row[\"status\"] == \"Completed\" and row[\"completed_steps\"] == row[\"total_steps\"] for row in rec[\"buildHistoryAfter\"]), \"Image build did not fully complete\")\n        raw = self.command(rec[\"commands\"][\"image\"], inv[\"command\"], self.path(cfg[\"receipt\"][\"path\"]).parent, inv[\"wholeCommandTimeoutSeconds\"])\n        result = image_summary(raw, self.head)\n        result.update(includeUnfixed=True, databaseUpdatesEnabled=True,\n                      sourceMapsAndSbom=\"Silent nonempty checks bound to reviewed canonical script and successful command; temporary files not re-read\")\n        review = self.document(cfg[\"review\"])\n        self.identity(review)\n        require(review[\"passed\"] is True and review[\"receiptSha256\"] == cfg[\"receipt\"][\"sha256\"] and review[\"logSha256\"] == rec[\"commands\"][\"image\"][\"sha256\"], \"Image review binding mismatch\")\n        require(all(review[key] == result[key] for key in (\"runtimeBytes\", \"manifest\", \"config\", \"targets\", \"highCriticalVulnerabilities\", \"includeUnfixed\", \"databaseUpdatesEnabled\")), \"Image review/raw summary mismatch\")\n        require(review[\"sourceCleanBeforeAfter\"] is True and review[\"ownedImageAndGroupAbsent\"] is True, \"Image review cleanup incomplete\")\n        self.results[\"image\"] = result\n\n    def combined(self):\n        descriptor = self.spec[\"combined\"]\n        rec = self.document(descriptor)\n        self.identity(rec)\n        require(rec[\"tools\"] == TOOLS and rec[\"sourceCleanBeforeAfter\"] is True, \"Combined source identity/tool mismatch\")\n        for item in rec[\"evidence\"].values():\n            self.document(item)\n        self.retained(rec)\n        require(self.same_binding(rec[\"evidence\"][\"sourceRunner\"], self.spec[\"source\"][\"receipt\"])\n                and self.same_binding(rec[\"evidence\"][\"source\"], self.spec[\"source\"][\"evidence\"])\n                and self.same_binding(rec[\"evidence\"][\"imageRunner\"], self.spec[\"image\"][\"receipt\"])\n                and self.same_binding(rec[\"evidence\"][\"image\"], self.spec[\"image\"][\"review\"]), \"Combined evidence identity mismatch\")\n        require(set(rec[\"gates\"]) == set(self.document(self.spec[\"source\"][\"receipt\"])[\"commands\"]) | {\"postgres\", \"image\"}, \"Combined gate set mismatch\")\n        for gate in rec[\"gates\"].values():\n            require(gate[\"passed\"] is True, \"Combined gate is not passed\")\n        evidence = self.document(self.spec[\"source\"][\"evidence\"])\n        require(all(rec[\"gates\"][name] == gate for name, gate in evidence[\"gates\"].items()), \"Combined source gates differ from source evidence\")\n        for name in (\"server\", \"app\"):\n            require(all(rec[\"gates\"][name][key] == value for key, value in self.results[\"source\"][name].items()), \"Combined unit summary mismatch\")\n        pg = rec[\"gates\"][\"postgres\"]\n        require(all(pg[key] == self.results[\"postgres\"][key] for key in (\"files\", \"tests\", \"cleanupReadback\")) and pg[\"allCollectedPassed\"] is True, \"Combined PostgreSQL summary mismatch\")\n        image_review = self.document(self.spec[\"image\"][\"review\"])\n        require(all(key in image_review and value == image_review[key] for key, value in rec[\"gates\"][\"image\"].items()), \"Combined image summary differs from image review\")\n        require(self.same_binding(rec[\"evidence\"][\"postgres\"], self.document(self.spec[\"image\"][\"invocation\"])[\"postgresEvidence\"])\n                and self.same_binding(rec[\"evidence\"][\"postgresCleanup\"], self.document(self.spec[\"image\"][\"invocation\"])[\"postgresCleanup\"]), \"Combined PostgreSQL binding mismatch\")\n\n    def runtime(self):\n        cfg = self.spec[\"runtime\"]\n        rec, plan = self.document(cfg[\"receipt\"]), self.document(cfg[\"plan\"])\n        self.identity(rec)\n        require(rec[\"status\"] == \"passed\" and rec[\"errors\"] == [] and rec[\"runnerSha256\"] == RUNTIME_V2_SHA,\n                \"Only successful normal v2 runtime receipts are supported; failed00 requires separate review\")\n        self.read(cfg[\"runner\"], RUNTIME_V2_SHA)\n        require(rec[\"planSha256\"] == cfg[\"plan\"][\"sha256\"] and plan[\"runnerSha256\"] == RUNTIME_V2_SHA, \"Runtime plan binding mismatch\")\n        self.document(plan[\"inventory\"])\n        require(rec[\"inventorySha256\"] == plan[\"inventory\"][\"sha256\"], \"Runtime inventory binding mismatch\")\n        entries = [row for row in plan[\"entries\"] if row[\"head\"] == self.head]\n        require(len(entries) == 1, \"Runtime target is not uniquely admitted\")\n        entry = entries[0]\n        self.identity(entry)\n        require(isinstance(entry[\"layerLabel\"], str) and re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9]{2}[a-z]?\", entry[\"layerLabel\"]), \"Missing or invalid layer label\")\n        require(re.fullmatch(re.escape(\"evorto-prefix-\" + entry[\"layerLabel\"] + \"-\" + self.head[:8] + \"-\") + r\"[a-z0-9]{1,8}\", rec[\"project\"]), \"Runtime project/layer identity mismatch\")\n        require(entry[\"ordinaryReceipt\"] == self.spec[\"combined\"][\"path\"] and entry[\"receiptSha256\"] == self.spec[\"combined\"][\"sha256\"], \"Runtime ordinary prerequisite mismatch\")\n        approval = self.document({\"path\": entry[\"readinessApproval\"], \"sha256\": entry[\"readinessApprovalSha256\"]})\n        self.identity(approval)\n        require(approval[\"status\"] == \"approved\" and approval[\"ordinaryReceiptSha256\"] == self.spec[\"combined\"][\"sha256\"]\n                and approval[\"runnerSha256\"] == RUNTIME_V2_SHA and approval[\"slotGrant\"] == rec[\"slotGrant\"], \"Runtime readiness approval mismatch\")\n        require(rec[\"ordinaryReceiptCountValidated\"] == len(plan[\"entries\"]) and rec[\"registeredPrefixCountValidated\"] == len(plan[\"registeredPrefixes\"])\n                and rec[\"historicalReceiptCountValidated\"] == len(plan[\"historicalOrdinaryEntries\"]), \"Runtime plan validation counts mismatch\")\n        require(plan[\"commands\"] == RUNTIME_COMMANDS and plan[\"noAutomaticRetry\"] is True, \"Runtime canonical command policy mismatch\")\n        require(plan[\"nodeVersion\"] == TOOLS[\"node\"] and plan[\"bunVersion\"] == TOOLS[\"bun\"], \"Runtime pinned tools mismatch\")\n        self.scripts(entry[\"canonicalScripts\"])\n        for key in (\"sourceSelected\", \"sourceAfter\"):\n            self.identity(rec[key], clean=True)\n        require(rec[\"sourceBeforeSelection\"][\"status\"] == \"\", \"Runtime started from dirty source\")\n        require(rec[\"trackedFileReadability\"] == {\"unreadableCount\": 0, \"paths\": []}, \"Runtime source readability failed\")\n        expected = {\"checkout\": [\"git\", \"switch\", \"--detach\", self.head], **{k:v for k,v in RUNTIME_COMMANDS.items() if k != \"runtime\"}}\n        require(list(rec[\"commands\"]) == list(expected), \"Runtime has missing/repeated/recovery commands\")\n        results = {}\n        directory = self.path(cfg[\"receipt\"][\"path\"]).parent\n        for name, command in expected.items():\n            item = rec[\"commands\"][name]\n            raw = self.command(item, command, directory, 1200 if name in (\"functional\", \"documentation\") else 300)\n            if name in (\"functional\", \"documentation\"):\n                result = playwright_summary(raw)\n                require(item[\"collected\"] == item[\"passed\"] == [result[\"tests\"]] and item[\"incompleteSummaryCount\"] == 0 and item[\"allCollectedPassed\"] is True, \"Runtime/raw summary mismatch\")\n                results[name] = result\n        runtime = rec[\"runtime\"]\n        require(runtime[\"command\"] == RUNTIME_COMMANDS[\"runtime\"] and runtime[\"pgid\"] == runtime[\"pid\"], \"Runtime supervisor identity mismatch\")\n        raw = self.read(runtime[\"log\"], runtime[\"sha256\"], directory)\n        require(len(raw) == runtime[\"bytes\"], \"Runtime raw log size mismatch\")\n        identity = runtime[\"identity\"]\n        self.identity(identity)\n        require(identity[\"readinessStatus\"] == 204 and identity[\"project\"] == rec[\"project\"]\n                and identity[\"workingDirectory\"] == plan[\"proofCheckout\"] and rec[\"ports\"] == entry[\"ports\"], \"Runtime project/checkout/readiness mismatch\")\n        require(re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-f]{64}\", identity[\"containerId\"]) and re.fullmatch(r\"sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}\", identity[\"imageId\"]), \"Invalid container/image identity\")\n        cleanup = rec[\"cleanup\"]\n        empty = {\"containers\": [], \"networks\": [], \"volumes\": []}\n        require(cleanup[\"errors\"] == [] and cleanup[\"remainingResources\"] == empty and cleanup[\"portsReleased\"] is True\n                and \"afterRecoveryResources\" not in cleanup, \"Runtime cleanup failed or required recovery\")\n        supervisor = cleanup[\"supervisor\"]\n        require(supervisor[\"exitCode\"] in (0, -15, 143) and supervisor[\"signals\"] in ([], [\"SIGTERM\"])\n                and supervisor[\"wasAlreadyExited\"] is False and supervisor[\"processGroupAbsent\"] is True, \"Runtime supervisor shutdown was not normal\")\n        self.probes(supervisor[\"groupProbeDiagnostics\"])\n        self.probes(cleanup[\"groupProbeDiagnostics\"])\n        if \"review\" in cfg:\n            review = self.document(cfg[\"review\"])\n            self.identity(review)\n            require(review[\"receiptSha256\"] == cfg[\"receipt\"][\"sha256\"] and review[\"ordinaryReceiptSha256\"] == self.spec[\"combined\"][\"sha256\"], \"Runtime review binding mismatch\")\n            require(review[\"functionalTests\"] == results[\"functional\"][\"tests\"] and review[\"documentationTests\"] == results[\"documentation\"][\"tests\"] and review[\"allCollectedPassed\"] is True and review[\"noRetries\"] is True, \"Runtime review summaries mismatch\")\n            require(review[\"cleanup\"] == cleanup and review[\"runtimeIdentity\"] == identity and review[\"cleanSourceBeforeAfter\"] is True\n                    and review[\"currentResources\"] == empty and review[\"currentPortsClosed\"] is True, \"Runtime review cleanup mismatch\")\n            require(set(review[\"currentOwnedProcessGroupsAbsent\"]) == {runtime[\"pgid\"], *(item[\"pgid\"] for item in rec[\"commands\"].values())}, \"Runtime reviewed process groups mismatch\")\n        self.results[\"runtime\"] = results\n\n    def verify(self):\n        require(self.git(\"rev-parse\", self.head + \"^{tree}\").decode().strip() == self.tree, \"Committed head/tree mismatch\")\n        self.source()\n        if \"image\" in self.spec:\n            self.image()\n        if \"combined\" in self.spec:\n            require(\"image\" in self.spec, \"Combined proof requires image inputs\")\n            self.combined()\n        if \"runtime\" in self.spec:\n            require(\"combined\" in self.spec, \"Runtime proof requires combined ordinary proof\")\n            self.runtime()\n        return self.results\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--input\", required=True, type=Path)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--output\", required=True, type=Path)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    require(not args.output.exists(), \"Refusing to replace an existing result\")\n    spec_raw = args.input.read_bytes()\n    verifier = None\n    result = {\"status\": \"failed\", \"inputSha256\": hashlib.sha256(spec_raw).hexdigest(),\n              \"verifierSha256\": hashlib.sha256(Path(__file__).read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n              \"checkedAt\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n              \"scope\": \"Offline evidence consistency only; no gate execution, current liveness proof, or approval\"}\n    try:\n        verifier = Verifier(decode(spec_raw))\n        result.update(head=verifier.head, tree=verifier.tree, gates=verifier.verify(), status=\"verified\")\n    except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError, OSError, UnicodeError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as error:\n        result[\"error\"] = {\"type\": type(error).__name__, \"reason\": str(error)}\n    if verifier:\n        result[\"verifiedFiles\"] = verifier.files\n    args.output.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    with args.output.open(\"x\") as handle:\n        json.dump(result, handle, indent=2)\n        handle.write(\"\\n\")\n    args.output.chmod(0o600)\n    print(json.dumps({\"status\": result[\"status\"], \"output\": str(args.output)}))\n    return 0 if result[\"status\"] == \"verified\" else 1\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3583},"formatted_output":"# Prefix result verifier proposal\n\n`verify_results.py` verifies saved successful source, image and normal v2 runtime receipts. It does not execute gates, approve a prefix, inspect current processes/services, change refs, or repair evidence. Root review is required before operational use.\n\nRun with an explicit input manifest and a **new** output filename:\n\n```sh\npython3 prefix-runtime-verification/result-verifier-proposal/verify_results.py \\\n  --input prefix-runtime-verification/result-verifier-proposal/inputs/successful-01-v2.json \\\n  --output /absolute/path/to/a/new/result.json\n```\n\nThe output is `verified` with exit 0 only if every requested stage passes. Unknown formats, missing bindings, failed receipts, mismatched hashes and unsupported commands fail with exit 1. Existing output files are never replaced. Only read-only `git rev-parse` and `git show` subprocesses are used; the active checkout can belong to another prefix.\n\n## Input and checks\n\nThe example manifest supplies `reviewRoot`, `gitRepository`, full `head`/`tree`, and explicit `{path, sha256}` descriptors. `source` is required; `image`, `combined` and `runtime` may be added as their actual evidence becomes available. Image requires its source-evidence descriptor; combined requires image; runtime requires combined. Relative paths resolve within the review artifact root. Rebind the manifest to each exact prefix; never relabel a historical result.\n\n- **Source:** committed head/tree/parent; clean recorded before/after identities; pinned Node 24.15.0/Bun 1.3.14; invocation, runner and reviewed ownership-helper hashes; exact ordered invocation commands with no missing/extra gates; zero exits and absent command groups; raw-log hash/size; canonical package scripts and declared source/probe hashes. Both full Vitest summaries must occur once with positive equal passed/collected counts and no incomplete/retry/error summary. The actual layer 15 `types` and `tooling-lint` commands are supported through its declared probes, strict root set/options and diagnostic artifacts. Unknown extra command names fail.\n- **Image:** successful canonical command, exact revision tag, strict unfixed/update flags, clean source, positive tag absence before/after, completed builds and absent process group. The raw runtime-size line and complete wrapped Trivy table are parsed; every target must report zero findings. Exported manifest/config and all parsed values must match the root review and combined evidence. Two reviewed image-check script hashes are pinned because their source-map and SPDX nonempty checks are silent. If either script changes, obtain a source review and update the allowlist deliberately.\n- **PostgreSQL prerequisite:** exact identity, full unselected canonical command with exit 0, complete raw Vitest counts, same cleanup container, and all recorded scoped cleanup counters zero. The existing standalone PG receipt does not record a process group; the result explicitly leaves that proof uncertified.\n- **Runtime:** only `status: passed` from the reviewed v2 runner; exact immutable plan snapshot, inventory, admitted `layerLabel`/canonical scripts, readiness approval and combined prerequisite; exact checkout/install/full functional/full docs sequence; each raw-log hash/size and complete Playwright summary; runtime project/checkout/container/image/readiness identities; normal supervisor exit, group absence, empty resources and released ports. Failed layer 00 plus its exceptional cleanup supplement is deliberately unsupported. Preparation failures before execution do not become test retries; acceptance still requires the later actual successful receipt and exact accepted plan.\n\nAll bound raw logs in this prefix's supplied receipt chain are rehashed, including PostgreSQL and runtime-supervisor logs. The helper does not repeat the separate historical inventory audit across other prefixes. Recorded cleanup and source snapshots are evidence of the original run, not a fresh live-state census. It does not claim exported temporary archives still exist after canonical cleanup.\n\n## Offline comparison\n\n`dry-run-01/final.json` verifies the unchanged successful 01 records: **33 evidence files / 15 raw logs**, server **168 files / 1,351 tests**, app **111 / 802**, PG **14 / 55**, functional **151**, docs **52**, runtime image **95,708,630 bytes**, **297 targets / 0 HIGH or CRITICAL findings**. No application/provider/DB/runtime/compile command was run.\n\n`compare_offline.py` uses the real 01 logs and in-memory alterations. Its 17 rejection cases cover partial/duplicate/mismatched summaries, retry/flaky output, unknown/unscanned Trivy output, wrong identity, dirty source, changed hash, nonzero exit, live groups, unresolved EPERM and a failed runtime with otherwise green tests. The original evidence is never edited. The supplemental layer 15 parsers are source-adapted to its current invocation; fresh layer 15 outputs are still pending and are not claimed verified here.\n\nEarlier dry-run outputs remain: attempt 1 rejected a wrapped Trivy row until the exact continuation format was supported; attempt 2 rejected a newly changed live runtime plan. The corrected input uses root's immutable `plan-replayed-v2-before02.json`, whose hash exactly matches the 01 execution receipt. Attempts 3/4 and final passed. These are verifier development runs, never application test retries.\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Offline receipt verifier. Reads evidence/Git objects; never runs a gate or repairs evidence.\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\n\nTOOLS = {\"node\": \"v24.15.0\", \"bun\": \"1.3.14\"}\nOWNERSHIP_SHA = \"820f0fdd78f77d8cd3dc98586d661b58c1b86d10847c9b2b3d07d1f4253b2215\"\nRUNTIME_V2_SHA = \"b12d86b81a1e66ad8b3777deb5c62a74a8606ec39d925b66a6ab41ab5c3f65c2\"\n# Changes to these two silent-check scripts need a new source review, not substring guesses.\nIMAGE_CHECKS = {\n    \"ops/scaleway/verify-image-security.sh\": \"f56ca53d08227eb0623f2b32954aadc39ccdb09cbb16627a27682c23a0eb1df9\",\n    \"ops/scaleway/verify-runtime-image.sh\": \"d2e887a8481baaa9e787eb443ff23cc3f0550fe1e905ff1e6faae82c5770f972\",\n}\nSOURCE_COMMANDS = {\n    \"install\": [\"bun\", \"install\", \"--frozen-lockfile\"],\n    \"release\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"release:validate\"],\n    \"format\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"format:check\"],\n    \"lint\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"lint\"],\n    \"clean-diff\": [\"git\", \"diff\", \"--exit-code\"],\n    \"server\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"test:unit:server\"],\n    \"app\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"test:unit\"],\n    \"infra\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"infra:check\"],\n}\nRUNTIME_COMMANDS = {\n    \"install\": SOURCE_COMMANDS[\"install\"],\n    \"runtime\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"docker:webserver\"],\n    \"functional\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"test:e2e\"],\n    \"documentation\": [\"bun\", \"run\", \"test:e2e:docs\"],\n}\nANSI = re.compile(r\"\\x1b\\[[0-?]*[ -/]*[@-~]\")\n\n\ndef require(condition, message):\n    if not condition:\n        raise ValueError(message)\n\n\ndef integer(value, minimum=0):\n    return type(value) is int and value >= minimum\n\n\ndef unique_object(pairs):\n    value = {}\n    for key, item in pairs:\n        require(key not in value, \"Duplicate JSON key\")\n        value[key] = item\n    return value\n\n\ndef decode(raw):\n    return json.loads(raw, object_pairs_hook=unique_object)\n\n\ndef unit_summary(raw):\n    text = ANSI.sub(\"\", raw)\n    result = {}\n    for label, key in ((\"Test Files\", \"files\"), (\"Tests\", \"tests\")):\n        lines = re.findall(r\"(?m)^\\s*\" + label + r\"\\s+([^\\n]+)$\", text)\n        require(len(lines) == 1, \"Missing or multiple Vitest \" + label + \" summaries\")\n        match = re.fullmatch(r\"(\\d+) passed \\((\\d+)\\)\\s*\", lines[0])\n        require(match is not None, \"Incomplete or unknown Vitest \" + label + \" summary\")\n        passed, collected = map(int, match.groups())\n        require(passed == collected and passed > 0, \"Vitest collection was not entirely successful\")\n        result[key] = collected\n    require(len(re.findall(r\"(?m)^\\s*Duration\\s+\\d\", text)) == 1, \"Missing or multiple Vitest completion lines\")\n    require(not re.search(r\"(?mi)^\\s*(?:Errors\\s+\\d|Unhandled Errors|FAIL\\b|Retry #\\d)|\\(retry #\\d|^\\s*\\d+ (?:failed|skipped|flaky|interrupted|todo|fixme)\\b\", text),\n            \"Vitest error or retry output\")\n    return result\n\n\ndef playwright_summary(raw):\n    text = ANSI.sub(\"\", raw)\n    collected = re.findall(r\"(?m)^Running (\\d+) tests? using \\d+ workers?\\s*$\", text)\n    passed = re.findall(r\"(?m)^\\s*(\\d+) passed \\([^\\n]+\\)\\s*$\", text)\n    require(len(collected) == len(passed) == 1 and collected == passed and int(passed[0]) > 0,\n            \"Incomplete, duplicate or unknown Playwright summary\")\n    require(not re.search(r\"(?mi)^\\s*\\d+ (?:failed|skipped|flaky|interrupted|did not run|expected failures?|todo|fixme)\\b|^\\s*Retry #\\d|\\(retry #\\d\", text),\n            \"Playwright incomplete or retry summary\")\n    return {\"tests\": int(passed[0]), \"allCollectedPassed\": True}\n\n\ndef image_summary(raw, head):\n    text = ANSI.sub(\"\", raw)\n    sizes = re.findall(r\"(?m)^Runtime image verification passed \\((\\d+) bytes\\)\\.$\", text)\n    require(len(sizes) == 1 and 0 < int(sizes[0]) < 1_000_000_000, \"Unknown runtime image size proof\")\n    require(text.count(\"Report Summary\") == 1, \"Unknown or duplicate Trivy report\")\n    table = text.split(\"Report Summary\", 1)[1]\n    require(\"Legend:\" in table, \"Truncated Trivy report\")\n    rows = [line.strip().split(\"│\")[1:-1] for line in table.splitlines() if line.strip().startswith(\"│\")]\n    rows = [[cell.strip() for cell in row] for row in rows]\n    require(rows and rows[0] == [\"Target\", \"Type\", \"Vulnerabilities\", \"Secrets\"], \"Unknown Trivy table schema\")\n    targets = []\n    for row in rows[1:]:\n        require(len(row) == 4, \"Unknown Trivy column count\")\n        if row[1:] == [\"\", \"\", \"\"]:\n            require(bool(targets) and bool(row[0]), \"Orphan Trivy target continuation\")\n            targets[-1][0] += row[0]\n        else:\n            targets.append(row)\n    require(bool(targets), \"Empty Trivy report\")\n    require(all(len(row) == 4 and row[0] and row[1] and row[2:] == [\"0\", \"-\"] for row in targets),\n            \"Unscanned, nonzero or unknown Trivy target\")\n    require(len({row[0] for row in targets}) == len(targets), \"Duplicate Trivy targets\")\n    require(targets[0][0].startswith(\"evorto-local-security:\" + head + \" (\"), \"Trivy image identity mismatch\")\n    result = {\"runtimeBytes\": int(sizes[0]), \"targets\": len(targets), \"highCriticalVulnerabilities\": 0}\n    for key in (\"manifest\", \"config\"):\n        matches = re.findall(r\"(?m)^#\\d+ exporting \" + key + r\" (sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}) done$\", text)\n        require(len(matches) == 1, \"Unknown image export \" + key)\n        result[key] = matches[0]\n    return result\n\n\nclass Verifier:\n    def __init__(self, specification):\n        self.spec = specification\n        self.review = Path(specification[\"reviewRoot\"]).resolve()\n        self.repo = Path(specification[\"gitRepository\"]).resolve()\n        self.head, self.tree = specification[\"head\"], specification[\"tree\"]\n        require(re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-f]{40}\", self.head) and re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-f]{40}\", self.tree), \"Expected full Git identities\")\n        self.files = {}\n        self.results = {}\n\n    def path(self, value, base=None):\n        path = Path(value)\n        if not path.is_absolute():\n            path = (base or self.review) / path\n        require(not path.is_symlink(), \"Evidence file is a symlink\")\n        path = path.resolve()\n        require(path.is_relative_to(self.review) and path.is_file(), \"Evidence file is missing or outside review root\")\n        return path\n\n    def read(self, value, expected=None, base=None):\n        path = self.path(value, base)\n        raw = path.read_bytes()\n        digest = hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()\n        if expected is not None:\n            require(re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-f]{64}\", expected) and digest == expected, \"Evidence hash mismatch: \" + str(path.relative_to(self.review)))\n        self.files[str(path.relative_to(self.review))] = {\"sha256\": digest, \"bytes\": len(raw)}\n        return raw\n\n    def same_binding(self, left, right):\n        return self.path(left[\"path\"]) == self.path(right[\"path\"]) and left[\"sha256\"] == right[\"sha256\"]\n\n    def document(self, descriptor):\n        return decode(self.read(descriptor[\"path\"], descriptor[\"sha256\"]))\n\n    def git(self, *args):\n        # Read committed objects only. Do not query or mutate the active checkout.\n        result = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"--no-optional-locks\", \"-C\", str(self.repo), *args],\n                                capture_output=True, timeout=30)\n        require(result.returncode == 0, \"Read-only Git object lookup failed\")\n        return result.stdout\n\n    def identity(self, value, clean=False):\n        require(value[\"head\"] == self.head and value[\"tree\"] == self.tree, \"Recorded head/tree mismatch\")\n        if clean:\n            require(value[\"status\"] == \"\", \"Recorded source is not clean\")\n\n    def envelope(self, receipt, invocation=None):\n        self.identity(receipt)\n        for key in (\"sourceBefore\", \"sourceAfter\"):\n            self.identity(receipt[key], clean=True)\n        require(receipt[\"errors\"] == [], \"Receipt records errors\")\n        require(receipt[\"tools\"] == TOOLS, \"Tool version mismatch\")\n        require(bool(receipt[\"slotGrant\"]) and receipt[\"slotGrant\"] != \"ACTUAL_ROOT_GRANT_REQUIRED\", \"Missing actual grant record\")\n        if invocation:\n            self.identity(invocation)\n            require(receipt[\"parent\"] == invocation[\"parent\"], \"Parent identity mismatch\")\n            require(self.git(\"rev-parse\", self.head + \"^\").decode().strip() == invocation[\"parent\"], \"Commit parent mismatch\")\n\n    def scripts(self, scripts, hashes=None):\n        package = decode(self.git(\"show\", self.head + \":package.json\"))\n        require(all(package[\"scripts\"][name] == command for name, command in scripts.items()), \"Canonical package script mismatch\")\n        for path, digest in (hashes or {}).items():\n            require(hashlib.sha256(self.git(\"show\", self.head + \":\" + path)).hexdigest() == digest,\n                    \"Bound canonical source hash mismatch: \" + path)\n\n    def probes(self, diagnostics):\n        require(isinstance(diagnostics, list), \"Unknown group-probe diagnostics\")\n        for probe in diagnostics:\n            require(probe[\"errno\"] == 1 and integer(probe[\"censusExitCode\"]) and probe[\"censusExitCode\"] == 0\n                    and type(probe[\"leaderExitCode\"]) is int and probe[\"remainingMemberPids\"] == []\n                    and probe[\"absenceConfirmedByNativeCensus\"] is True, \"Unresolved process-group probe\")\n\n    def command(self, item, expected, directory, bound):\n        require(item[\"command\"] == expected, \"Invocation/recorded command mismatch\")\n        require(item[\"status\"] == \"passed\" and type(item[\"exitCode\"]) is int and item[\"exitCode\"] == 0,\n                \"Command did not pass\")\n        require(not any(key in item for key in (\"error\", \"termination\", \"retry\", \"retries\")), \"Command termination/retry evidence\")\n        require(integer(item[\"pid\"], 1) and item[\"pgid\"] == item[\"pid\"] and item[\"processGroupAbsent\"] is True,\n                \"Command process-group cleanup not proven\")\n        self.probes(item.get(\"groupProbeDiagnostics\", []))\n        require(type(item[\"seconds\"]) in (int, float) and 0 <= item[\"seconds\"] <= bound, \"Command exceeded declared bound\")\n        raw = self.read(item[\"log\"], item[\"sha256\"], directory)\n        require(len(raw) == item[\"bytes\"], \"Raw log byte-count mismatch\")\n        return raw.decode(\"utf8\")\n\n    def retained(self, record):\n        for path, digest in record.get(\"retainedLogHashes\", {}).items():\n            self.read(path, digest)\n\n    def source(self):\n        cfg = self.spec[\"source\"]\n        inv, rec = self.document(cfg[\"invocation\"]), self.document(cfg[\"receipt\"])\n        self.envelope(rec, inv)\n        require(rec[\"status\"] in (\n            \"source-gates-passed; root PG and image acceptance pending\",\n            \"source-gates-passed; fresh root PG required before image/runtime preparation\"), \"Source receipt is not successful\")\n        require(rec[\"invocationSha256\"] == cfg[\"invocation\"][\"sha256\"], \"Source invocation binding mismatch\")\n        self.read(inv[\"sourceCommand\"][1], rec[\"runnerSha256\"])\n        require(rec[\"helperSha256\"] == OWNERSHIP_SHA, \"Unreviewed source ownership helper\")\n        self.read(cfg[\"ownershipHelper\"], OWNERSHIP_SHA)\n        require(inv[\"requiredVersions\"] == TOOLS, \"Invocation tools mismatch\")\n        self.scripts(inv[\"canonicalSourceScripts\"], inv.get(\"sourceScriptFileHashes\"))\n        for artifact in inv.get(\"boundExternalArtifacts\", []):\n            self.read(artifact[\"path\"], artifact[\"sha256\"])\n        steps = inv[\"commands\"]\n        require([step[\"name\"] for step in steps] == list(rec[\"commands\"]), \"Missing, repeated or reordered source command\")\n        require(set(SOURCE_COMMANDS) <= set(rec[\"commands\"]), \"Missing required source gate\")\n        results = {}\n        directory = self.path(cfg[\"receipt\"][\"path\"]).parent\n        for step in steps:\n            name, command = step[\"name\"], step[\"command\"]\n            require(name in SOURCE_COMMANDS or name in (\"types\", \"tooling-lint\"), \"Unreviewed additional source gate\")\n            if name in SOURCE_COMMANDS:\n                require(command == SOURCE_COMMANDS[name], \"Noncanonical source command\")\n            raw = self.command(rec[\"commands\"][name], command, directory, inv[\"processTimeoutSeconds\"])\n            if name in (\"server\", \"app\"):\n                results[name] = unit_summary(raw)\n            elif name == \"clean-diff\":\n                require(raw == \"\", \"Clean diff contains output\")\n            elif name == \"format\":\n                require(\"All matched files use Prettier code style!\" in raw, \"Unknown format success output\")\n            elif name in (\"types\", \"tooling-lint\"):\n                self.extra_source(name, raw, command, inv, directory, results)\n        if \"evidence\" in cfg:\n            evidence = self.document(cfg[\"evidence\"])\n            self.identity(evidence)\n            require(evidence[\"sourceBefore\"] == rec[\"sourceBefore\"] and evidence[\"sourceAfter\"] == rec[\"sourceAfter\"]\n                    and evidence[\"tools\"] == rec[\"tools\"] and evidence[\"sourceRunnerReceiptSha256\"] == cfg[\"receipt\"][\"sha256\"], \"Source review binding mismatch\")\n            require(set(evidence[\"gates\"]) == set(rec[\"commands\"]), \"Source review gate set mismatch\")\n            for name, gate in evidence[\"gates\"].items():\n                command = rec[\"commands\"][name]\n                require(gate[\"passed\"] is True and gate[\"command\"] == command[\"command\"] and gate[\"sha256\"] == command[\"sha256\"], \"Source review gate mismatch\")\n                self.read(gate[\"log\"], gate[\"sha256\"])\n                if name in (\"server\", \"app\"):\n                    require(all(gate[k] == v for k, v in results[name].items()) and gate[\"allCollectedPassed\"] is True and gate[\"incompleteSummaries\"] == [], \"Source review summary mismatch\")\n            self.retained(evidence)\n        self.results[\"source\"] = results\n        return inv\n\n    def extra_source(self, name, raw, command, inv, directory, results):\n        require(command[0] == \"node\" and len(command) == 2, \"Unknown supplemental command shape\")\n        descriptor = inv[\"strictGraph\" if name == \"types\" else \"supplementalToolingLint\"]\n        probe = descriptor[\"preparedProbe\"]\n        require(command[1] == probe[\"path\"], \"Supplemental probe mismatch\")\n        self.read(probe[\"path\"], probe[\"sha256\"])\n        value = decode(raw.strip())\n        if name == \"types\":\n            require(value[\"diagnostics\"] == 0 and value[\"strict\"] is True and integer(value[\"roots\"], 1)\n                    and integer(value[\"firstPartySources\"], value[\"roots\"]), \"Strict summary is not successful\")\n            roots = decode(self.read(directory / \"roots.json\"))\n            expected = decode(self.read(descriptor[\"expectedRootSet\"][\"path\"], descriptor[\"expectedRootSet\"][\"sha256\"]))\n            require(roots == expected == descriptor[\"rootNames\"] and len(roots) == value[\"roots\"] == descriptor[\"expectedRootCount\"], \"Actual strict roots differ from invocation\")\n            require(value[\"skipLibCheck\"] == descriptor[\"compilerConfiguration\"][\"inheritedSkipLibCheck\"], \"Strict compiler options mismatch\")\n            require(decode(self.read(directory / \"diagnostics.json\")) == [], \"Strict diagnostics artifact is nonempty\")\n            results[name] = value\n        else:\n            require(isinstance(value, list) and len(value) == len(descriptor[\"rootNames\"]), \"Unknown tooling summary\")\n            require({str(Path(item[\"filePath\"]).relative_to(inv[\"proofCheckout\"])) for item in value} == set(descriptor[\"rootNames\"]), \"Tooling root set mismatch\")\n            require(all(all(item[key] == 0 for key in (\"errorCount\", \"warningCount\", \"fatalErrorCount\")) for item in value), \"Tooling warnings/errors present\")\n            results[name] = {\"files\": len(value), \"errors\": 0, \"warnings\": 0}\n\n    def postgres(self, descriptor, cleanup_descriptor):\n        rec, cleanup = self.document(descriptor), self.document(cleanup_descriptor)\n        self.identity(rec)\n        for key in (\"sourceBefore\", \"sourceAfter\"):\n            self.identity(rec[key], clean=True)\n        require(rec[\"status\"] == \"passed\" and rec[\"exitCode\"] == 0 and rec[\"command\"] == [\"bun\", \"run\", \"test:integration:postgres\"], \"PostgreSQL gate failed or selected\")\n        result = unit_summary(self.read(rec[\"log\"], rec[\"sha256\"]).decode())\n        require(cleanup[\"containerId\"] == rec[\"databaseContainerId\"], \"PostgreSQL cleanup owner mismatch\")\n        counts = cleanup[\"readback\"]\n        require(set(counts) >= {\"urlRaceTenants\", \"concurrencyTenants\", \"idleInTransaction\", \"activeClientQueries\"}\n                and all(type(value) is int and value == 0 for value in counts.values()), \"PostgreSQL cleanup readback is not zero\")\n        result[\"cleanupReadback\"] = counts\n        result[\"processGroupEvidence\"] = \"Not recorded by this standalone PostgreSQL receipt; not independently certified\"\n        self.results[\"postgres\"] = result\n\n    def image(self):\n        cfg = self.spec[\"image\"]\n        inv, rec = self.document(cfg[\"invocation\"]), self.document(cfg[\"receipt\"])\n        self.envelope(rec, inv)\n        require(rec[\"status\"] == \"passed\" and rec[\"invocationSha256\"] == cfg[\"invocation\"][\"sha256\"], \"Image receipt/invocation failed\")\n        self.read(cfg[\"runner\"], rec[\"runnerSha256\"])\n        require(rec[\"ownershipHelperSha256\"] == OWNERSHIP_SHA, \"Unreviewed image ownership helper\")\n        self.read(cfg[\"ownershipHelper\"], OWNERSHIP_SHA)\n        for key in (\"sourceEvidence\", \"postgresEvidence\", \"postgresCleanup\"):\n            self.document(inv[key])\n        require(self.same_binding(inv[\"sourceEvidence\"], self.spec[\"source\"][\"evidence\"]), \"Image/source evidence binding mismatch\")\n        self.postgres(inv[\"postgresEvidence\"], inv[\"postgresCleanup\"])\n        self.scripts({\"image:security:local\": inv[\"script\"]}, inv[\"canonicalSourceHashes\"])\n        require(all(inv[\"canonicalSourceHashes\"].get(key) == digest for key, digest in IMAGE_CHECKS.items()), \"Image silent-check script needs fresh review\")\n        require(inv[\"command\"] == [\"bun\", \"run\", \"image:security:local\"] and list(rec[\"commands\"]) == [\"image\"], \"Image retry/recovery/noncanonical command\")\n        require(inv[\"image\"] == \"evorto-local-security:\" + self.head, \"Image tag identity mismatch\")\n        require(rec[\"environment\"] == inv[\"environment\"], \"Image environment mismatch\")\n        require(all(inv[\"environment\"].get(key) == value for key, value in {\"CI\": \"true\", \"TRIVY_IGNORE_UNFIXED\": \"false\", \"TRIVY_SKIP_DB_UPDATE\": \"false\"}.items()), \"Image scan is not strict\")\n        for state in (rec[\"imageBefore\"], rec[\"cleanup\"][\"imageAfter\"]):\n            require(state[\"exists\"] is False and integer(state[\"exitCode\"], 1), \"Exact image absence was not proven\")\n        require(rec[\"cleanup\"][\"ownedCommandStarted\"] is True and \"afterRecovery\" not in rec[\"cleanup\"], \"Image cleanup required recovery\")\n        require(all(row[\"status\"] != \"Running\" for row in rec[\"buildHistoryBefore\"]), \"Image started alongside another build\")\n        require(rec[\"buildHistoryAfter\"] and all(row[\"status\"] == \"Completed\" and row[\"completed_steps\"] == row[\"total_steps\"] for row in rec[\"buildHistoryAfter\"]), \"Image build did not fully complete\")\n        raw = self.command(rec[\"commands\"][\"image\"], inv[\"command\"], self.path(cfg[\"receipt\"][\"path\"]).parent, inv[\"wholeCommandTimeoutSeconds\"])\n        result = image_summary(raw, self.head)\n        result.update(includeUnfixed=True, databaseUpdatesEnabled=True,\n                      sourceMapsAndSbom=\"Silent nonempty checks bound to reviewed canonical script and successful command; temporary files not re-read\")\n        review = self.document(cfg[\"review\"])\n        self.identity(review)\n        require(review[\"passed\"] is True and review[\"receiptSha256\"] == cfg[\"receipt\"][\"sha256\"] and review[\"logSha256\"] == rec[\"commands\"][\"image\"][\"sha256\"], \"Image review binding mismatch\")\n        require(all(review[key] == result[key] for key in (\"runtimeBytes\", \"manifest\", \"config\", \"targets\", \"highCriticalVulnerabilities\", \"includeUnfixed\", \"databaseUpdatesEnabled\")), \"Image review/raw summary mismatch\")\n        require(review[\"sourceCleanBeforeAfter\"] is True and review[\"ownedImageAndGroupAbsent\"] is True, \"Image review cleanup incomplete\")\n        self.results[\"image\"] = result\n\n    def combined(self):\n        descriptor = self.spec[\"combined\"]\n        rec = self.document(descriptor)\n        self.identity(rec)\n        require(rec[\"tools\"] == TOOLS and rec[\"sourceCleanBeforeAfter\"] is True, \"Combined source identity/tool mismatch\")\n        for item in rec[\"evidence\"].values():\n            self.document(item)\n        self.retained(rec)\n        require(self.same_binding(rec[\"evidence\"][\"sourceRunner\"], self.spec[\"source\"][\"receipt\"])\n                and self.same_binding(rec[\"evidence\"][\"source\"], self.spec[\"source\"][\"evidence\"])\n                and self.same_binding(rec[\"evidence\"][\"imageRunner\"], self.spec[\"image\"][\"receipt\"])\n                and self.same_binding(rec[\"evidence\"][\"image\"], self.spec[\"image\"][\"review\"]), \"Combined evidence identity mismatch\")\n        require(set(rec[\"gates\"]) == set(self.document(self.spec[\"source\"][\"receipt\"])[\"commands\"]) | {\"postgres\", \"image\"}, \"Combined gate set mismatch\")\n        for gate in rec[\"gates\"].values():\n            require(gate[\"passed\"] is True, \"Combined gate is not passed\")\n        evidence = self.document(self.spec[\"source\"][\"evidence\"])\n        require(all(rec[\"gates\"][name] == gate for name, gate in evidence[\"gates\"].items()), \"Combined source gates differ from source evidence\")\n        for name in (\"server\", \"app\"):\n            require(all(rec[\"gates\"][name][key] == value for key, value in self.results[\"source\"][name].items()), \"Combined unit summary mismatch\")\n        pg = rec[\"gates\"][\"postgres\"]\n        require(all(pg[key] == self.results[\"postgres\"][key] for key in (\"files\", \"tests\", \"cleanupReadback\")) and pg[\"allCollectedPassed\"] is True, \"Combined PostgreSQL summary mismatch\")\n        image_review = self.document(self.spec[\"image\"][\"review\"])\n        require(all(key in image_review and value == image_review[key] for key, value in rec[\"gates\"][\"image\"].items()), \"Combined image summary differs from image review\")\n        require(self.same_binding(rec[\"evidence\"][\"postgres\"], self.document(self.spec[\"image\"][\"invocation\"])[\"postgresEvidence\"])\n                and self.same_binding(rec[\"evidence\"][\"postgresCleanup\"], self.document(self.spec[\"image\"][\"invocation\"])[\"postgresCleanup\"]), \"Combined PostgreSQL binding mismatch\")\n\n    def runtime(self):\n        cfg = self.spec[\"runtime\"]\n        rec, plan = self.document(cfg[\"receipt\"]), self.document(cfg[\"plan\"])\n        self.identity(rec)\n        require(rec[\"status\"] == \"passed\" and rec[\"errors\"] == [] and rec[\"runnerSha256\"] == RUNTIME_V2_SHA,\n                \"Only successful normal v2 runtime receipts are supported; failed00 requires separate review\")\n        self.read(cfg[\"runner\"], RUNTIME_V2_SHA)\n        require(rec[\"planSha256\"] == cfg[\"plan\"][\"sha256\"] and plan[\"runnerSha256\"] == RUNTIME_V2_SHA, \"Runtime plan binding mismatch\")\n        self.document(plan[\"inventory\"])\n        require(rec[\"inventorySha256\"] == plan[\"inventory\"][\"sha256\"], \"Runtime inventory binding mismatch\")\n        entries = [row for row in plan[\"entries\"] if row[\"head\"] == self.head]\n        require(len(entries) == 1, \"Runtime target is not uniquely admitted\")\n        entry = entries[0]\n        self.identity(entry)\n        require(isinstance(entry[\"layerLabel\"], str) and re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9]{2}[a-z]?\", entry[\"layerLabel\"]), \"Missing or invalid layer label\")\n        require(re.fullmatch(re.escape(\"evorto-prefix-\" + entry[\"layerLabel\"] + \"-\" + self.head[:8] + \"-\") + r\"[a-z0-9]{1,8}\", rec[\"project\"]), \"Runtime project/layer identity mismatch\")\n        require(entry[\"ordinaryReceipt\"] == self.spec[\"combined\"][\"path\"] and entry[\"receiptSha256\"] == self.spec[\"combined\"][\"sha256\"], \"Runtime ordinary prerequisite mismatch\")\n        approval = self.document({\"path\": entry[\"readinessApproval\"], \"sha256\": entry[\"readinessApprovalSha256\"]})\n        self.identity(approval)\n        require(approval[\"status\"] == \"approved\" and approval[\"ordinaryReceiptSha256\"] == self.spec[\"combined\"][\"sha256\"]\n                and approval[\"runnerSha256\"] == RUNTIME_V2_SHA and approval[\"slotGrant\"] == rec[\"slotGrant\"], \"Runtime readiness approval mismatch\")\n        require(rec[\"ordinaryReceiptCountValidated\"] == len(plan[\"entries\"]) and rec[\"registeredPrefixCountValidated\"] == len(plan[\"registeredPrefixes\"])\n                and rec[\"historicalReceiptCountValidated\"] == len(plan[\"historicalOrdinaryEntries\"]), \"Runtime plan validation counts mismatch\")\n        require(plan[\"commands\"] == RUNTIME_COMMANDS and plan[\"noAutomaticRetry\"] is True, \"Runtime canonical command policy mismatch\")\n        require(plan[\"nodeVersion\"] == TOOLS[\"node\"] and plan[\"bunVersion\"] == TOOLS[\"bun\"], \"Runtime pinned tools mismatch\")\n        self.scripts(entry[\"canonicalScripts\"])\n        for key in (\"sourceSelected\", \"sourceAfter\"):\n            self.identity(rec[key], clean=True)\n        require(rec[\"sourceBeforeSelection\"][\"status\"] == \"\", \"Runtime started from dirty source\")\n        require(rec[\"trackedFileReadability\"] == {\"unreadableCount\": 0, \"paths\": []}, \"Runtime source readability failed\")\n        expected = {\"checkout\": [\"git\", \"switch\", \"--detach\", self.head], **{k:v for k,v in RUNTIME_COMMANDS.items() if k != \"runtime\"}}\n        require(list(rec[\"commands\"]) == list(expected), \"Runtime has missing/repeated/recovery commands\")\n        results = {}\n        directory = self.path(cfg[\"receipt\"][\"path\"]).parent\n        for name, command in expected.items():\n            item = rec[\"commands\"][name]\n            raw = self.command(item, command, directory, 1200 if name in (\"functional\", \"documentation\") else 300)\n            if name in (\"functional\", \"documentation\"):\n                result = playwright_summary(raw)\n                require(item[\"collected\"] == item[\"passed\"] == [result[\"tests\"]] and item[\"incompleteSummaryCount\"] == 0 and item[\"allCollectedPassed\"] is True, \"Runtime/raw summary mismatch\")\n                results[name] = result\n        runtime = rec[\"runtime\"]\n        require(runtime[\"command\"] == RUNTIME_COMMANDS[\"runtime\"] and runtime[\"pgid\"] == runtime[\"pid\"], \"Runtime supervisor identity mismatch\")\n        raw = self.read(runtime[\"log\"], runtime[\"sha256\"], directory)\n        require(len(raw) == runtime[\"bytes\"], \"Runtime raw log size mismatch\")\n        identity = runtime[\"identity\"]\n        self.identity(identity)\n        require(identity[\"readinessStatus\"] == 204 and identity[\"project\"] == rec[\"project\"]\n                and identity[\"workingDirectory\"] == plan[\"proofCheckout\"] and rec[\"ports\"] == entry[\"ports\"], \"Runtime project/checkout/readiness mismatch\")\n        require(re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-f]{64}\", identity[\"containerId\"]) and re.fullmatch(r\"sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}\", identity[\"imageId\"]), \"Invalid container/image identity\")\n        cleanup = rec[\"cleanup\"]\n        empty = {\"containers\": [], \"networks\": [], \"volumes\": []}\n        require(cleanup[\"errors\"] == [] and cleanup[\"remainingResources\"] == empty and cleanup[\"portsReleased\"] is True\n                and \"afterRecoveryResources\" not in cleanup, \"Runtime cleanup failed or required recovery\")\n        supervisor = cleanup[\"supervisor\"]\n        require(supervisor[\"exitCode\"] in (0, -15, 143) and supervisor[\"signals\"] in ([], [\"SIGTERM\"])\n                and supervisor[\"wasAlreadyExited\"] is False and supervisor[\"processGroupAbsent\"] is True, \"Runtime supervisor shutdown was not normal\")\n        self.probes(supervisor[\"groupProbeDiagnostics\"])\n        self.probes(cleanup[\"groupProbeDiagnostics\"])\n        if \"review\" in cfg:\n            review = self.document(cfg[\"review\"])\n            self.identity(review)\n            require(review[\"receiptSha256\"] == cfg[\"receipt\"][\"sha256\"] and review[\"ordinaryReceiptSha256\"] == self.spec[\"combined\"][\"sha256\"], \"Runtime review binding mismatch\")\n            require(review[\"functionalTests\"] == results[\"functional\"][\"tests\"] and review[\"documentationTests\"] == results[\"documentation\"][\"tests\"] and review[\"allCollectedPassed\"] is True and review[\"noRetries\"] is True, \"Runtime review summaries mismatch\")\n            require(review[\"cleanup\"] == cleanup and review[\"runtimeIdentity\"] == identity and review[\"cleanSourceBeforeAfter\"] is True\n                    and review[\"currentResources\"] == empty and review[\"currentPortsClosed\"] is True, \"Runtime review cleanup mismatch\")\n            require(set(review[\"currentOwnedProcessGroupsAbsent\"]) == {runtime[\"pgid\"], *(item[\"pgid\"] for item in rec[\"commands\"].values())}, \"Runtime reviewed process groups mismatch\")\n        self.results[\"runtime\"] = results\n\n    def verify(self):\n        require(self.git(\"rev-parse\", self.head + \"^{tree}\").decode().strip() == self.tree, \"Committed head/tree mismatch\")\n        self.source()\n        if \"image\" in self.spec:\n            self.image()\n        if \"combined\" in self.spec:\n            require(\"image\" in self.spec, \"Combined proof requires image inputs\")\n            self.combined()\n        if \"runtime\" in self.spec:\n            require(\"combined\" in self.spec, \"Runtime proof requires combined ordinary proof\")\n            self.runtime()\n        return self.results\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--input\", required=True, type=Path)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--output\", required=True, type=Path)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    require(not args.output.exists(), \"Refusing to replace an existing result\")\n    spec_raw = args.input.read_bytes()\n    verifier = None\n    result = {\"status\": \"failed\", \"inputSha256\": hashlib.sha256(spec_raw).hexdigest(),\n              \"verifierSha256\": hashlib.sha256(Path(__file__).read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n              \"checkedAt\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n              \"scope\": \"Offline evidence consistency only; no gate execution, current liveness proof, or approval\"}\n    try:\n        verifier = Verifier(decode(spec_raw))\n        result.update(head=verifier.head, tree=verifier.tree, gates=verifier.verify(), status=\"verified\")\n    except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError, OSError, UnicodeError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as error:\n        result[\"error\"] = {\"type\": type(error).__name__, \"reason\": str(error)}\n    if verifier:\n        result[\"verifiedFiles\"] = verifier.files\n    args.output.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    with args.output.open(\"x\") as handle:\n        json.dump(result, handle, indent=2)\n        handle.write(\"\\n\")\n    args.output.chmod(0o600)\n    print(json.dumps({\"status\": result[\"status\"], \"output\": str(args.output)}))\n    return 0 if result[\"status\"] == \"verified\" else 1\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n"},"started_at_ms":1788572288212,"completed_at_ms":1788572288212}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-05T01:38:08.237Z","ordinal":20519,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06cdc-629f-7b82-8a80-b940922d7571","turn_id":"01a06cdc-6399-7b30-9fa8-4b87f0cfba0e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3831ca56-6242-458f-949f-cb5c1fefff93","process_id":"20349","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat layer17b-event-discovery/final-parent-rebind/README.md && cat layer17b-event-discovery/final-parent-rebind/source-preparation-receipt.json"],"cwd":"file:///Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/aa9e/evorto-stack-review","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat layer17b-event-discovery/final-parent-rebind/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"layer17b-event-discovery/final-parent-rebind/README.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat layer17b-event-discovery/final-parent-rebind/source-preparation-receipt.json","name":"source-preparation-receipt.json","path":"layer17b-event-discovery/final-parent-rebind/source-preparation-receipt.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","stdout":"# Event discovery source rebind\n\nThis source-only candidate contains exactly83 owning paths on the frozen17A24 projection, derived from final15 plus accepted16S85 and16R45. The captured parent has1300 first-party files; actual16S/16R/17A branch heads and all canonical verification remain pending. No synthetic commit is claimed.\n\nSign-up events are discovered through eligible choices. Anonymous visitors use the default new-member roles, and published direct links remain readable without bypassing sign-in or sign-up requirements. Optionless announcements have explicit role targeting. Review permissions and tenant boundaries remain enforced by the current handlers. The UI explains discovery and sign-up states, keeps entered values across uncertain outcomes, and drains required reads before clearing action locks.\n\nThe rebind preserves final13 transactional transfer fixtures, final14 scanner contracts, final15 ESN/source mapping and F228/F231 editors,16S