 but its local `development` fallback is not revision proof: bind the running image to the recorded clean-source build. Root owns runtime, disposable seed data and cleanup. Use the pinned Node 24.15.0 and canonical worktree scripts.\n\nRun complete unfiltered `bun run test:e2e` and `bun run test:e2e:docs`. These existing cases cover the ordinary paths; selected cases alone are not the full gate:\n\n| Existing case and file | Coverage and remaining gap |\n| --- | --- |\n| **profile edit persists notification email and reimbursement details** — `tests/specs/profile/user-profile-edit.spec.ts`; **Manage your profile** — `tests/docs/profile/user-profile.doc.ts` | Validation, normal save, normalized persisted details and unchanged sign-in email. No uncertain response or delayed/failed follow-up read. |\n| **Join another organization and choose your home organization** — `tests/docs/users/tenant-onboarding.doc.ts` | Named confirmation, persisted home ID and old warning absent after reload. Does not assert the home field/warning update immediately before reload. |\n| **profile discounts show seeded ESNcard state and block invalid saves** — `tests/specs/profile/user-profile-discounts.spec.ts`; **Manage ESNcard** — `tests/docs/profile/discounts.doc.ts` | Seeded state and invalid input; no mutation/read recovery. |\n| **event authoring controls expose accessible names and keyboard interaction**, **create event form template**, **event edit form hides selected roles in autocomplete** — `tests/specs/events/events.test.ts` | Normal editor controls; no first-row deletion with surviving dirty values and one saved graph. |\n| **event list icon actions are named and keyboard operable** — `tests/specs/events/events.test.ts`; **Review and publish an event** — `tests/docs/events/event-approval.doc.ts` | Normal list/review navigation; no later-page failure or paused conflict read. |\n\nAdditional **Codex in-app Browser** checks, through visible navigation and controls:\n\n1. **Profile/home:** save edited details while holding one local follow-up read; verify fields, Save, Cancel and Escape stay locked until it settles. A confirmed save plus failed read must retain truthful saved copy and Close only; reopen to see persisted details. An unconfirmed response retains entries and asks the user to check before resubmitting. Change home organization once and check the profile's Home organization value and removal of its old warning/action **before reload**. A concurrent completed profile edit must not revert that home value. This concerns the profile field, not a separate Home page.\n2. **Cards:** remove an owned seeded card while holding/failing the following list read. Further writes remain blocked; Try again only reads, restores current state and then re-enables writes. Also check initial read recovery and retained input after an unconfirmed response. Provider save/check-again success remains covered by the existing active/expired journeys in `user-profile-live-esncard.spec.ts` and the live `discounts.doc.ts` case: schedule `bun run test:e2e:live-esncard:release` separately, without synthetic provider success.\n3. **F231 rows:** in an owned draft with several choices, questions and add-ons, edit a surviving row and remove the first row of each kind with its public button. Verify surviving controls/values, save once and reopen the graph. Include choice removal followed by the simple-mode confirmation. Check for console exceptions and duplicate writes.\n4. **F230 pagination:** after a real first page, fail only the next-page read. Existing links must remain usable beside the error and enabled Load more. Restore transport and load the next page once without duplicate entries. Preserve initial-load Try again behavior. This code is unchanged by this batch but still lacks fresh runtime acceptance.\n5. **Paused review:** on an owned event, retain a draft comment, receive an expected conflict and pause the follow-up read. Show the original conflict guidance without claiming fresh details; restore transport and recover normally. No announcement/discovery change is needed.\n\nFailure checks need scoped local request delay/failure while retaining real component/query state. Record action, outcome, relevant request counts, settled screenshot and console state. Own fixture cleanup before mutation; restore all data/interceptions/network settings, drain work and attempt every cleanup. An unavailable deterministic fixture/control leaves that manual check explicitly pending; actual-component unit proof remains separate.\n\n**No prior Browser credit for these changed behaviors.** `assembly-browser-event-details-505716.md` proves only anonymous normal forward navigation on `505716c`, predating the fixes. It does not close profile/card/cache, row-deletion or pagination-error acceptance. Fresh observations must bind to `56e7fdc`.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"status\": \"Existing Browser plan remains applicable to fixture-only successor; no runtime credit added\",\n  \"head\": \"16f2a0a36834569e19355592b44499de0bf129a1\",\n  \"base\": \"56e7fdc90802f8478b2d56eb6de88bf1db01bac7\",\n  \"plan\": \"assembly-56e7-browser-acceptance-plan.md\",\n  \"planSha256\": \"1325b4f33330f3bc756d309db657b121c873704f47d943a88a9f4f5c797d2d7d\",\n  \"changedPaths\": [\n    \"APPLICATION_REVIEW_QUEUE.md\",\n    \"src/server/effect/rpc/handlers/events/events-query.handlers.postgres.spec.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"allProductionSourceUnchanged\": true,\n  \"required\": \"Run fresh complete acceptance and manual Browser checks on the new clean assembly head\"\n}\n# Browser acceptance plan — 56e7fdc\n\n**Execution pending.** Source read: clean `56e7fdc90802f8478b2d56eb6de88bf1db01bac7`, tree `811989533a546642300de116e91822d053cd4576`, exact 14-path parent diff. Root reports 1,674 server / 1,342 app / 123 PostgreSQL tests passing.\n\nBuild fresh from this source, recording the image/container identity, build log, tenant/base URL and readiness result. Read `/v