{"timestamp":"2026-09-05T01:52:35.380Z","ordinal":20885,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a06cdc-629f-7b82-8a80-b940922d7571","turn_id":"01a06cdc-6399-7b30-9fa8-4b87f0cfba0e","session_id":"01a06cdc-629f-7b82-8a80-b940922d7571","root_turn_id":"01a06cdc-6399-7b30-9fa8-4b87f0cfba0e","response_id":"resp_0c5872428dbc2885016a9b75e044b887d282052729cb6eafc0","usage":{"input_tokens":115717,"cached_input_tokens":115584,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":83,"reasoning_output_tokens":24,"total_tokens":115800},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":299811971,"cached_input_tokens":295087104,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":974417,"reasoning_output_tokens":329836,"total_tokens":300786388},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":299811971,"cached_input_tokens":295087104,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":974417,"reasoning_output_tokens":329836,"total_tokens":300786388}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-05T01:52:35.385Z","ordinal":20886,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06cdc-629f-7b82-8a80-b940922d7571","turn_id":"01a06cdc-6399-7b30-9fa8-4b87f0cfba0e","item":{"type":"McpToolCall","id":"call_HdhSiquXNWHG5FYz2W7ep0IQ","server":"cua_repl","tool":"js","arguments":{"code":"let acceptanceCdp = await acceptanceTab.capabilities.get('cdp'); nodeRepl.write(await acceptanceCdp.documentation());","title":"Inspect supported local request-delay and failure controls"},"pluginId":"unified-computer-use@openai-bundled","readOnlyHint":true,"status":"completed","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Tab Capability: cdp\nRaw Chrome DevTools Protocol access in browser for development use. Prefer higher-level Browser Use APIs. Navigate a fresh tab to its intended HTTP or HTTPS page before the first CDP command. Raw CDP access is scoped to the tab's current web origin. To observe an action, call `readEvents()` to capture `cursor`, perform the action, then read from that cursor with `afterSequence`. Continue from each returned cursor while `hasMore` is true; `truncated` means older events were evicted. Reuse the same filters while paging. Discover child target selectors from `Target.attachedToTarget` events. If you directly modify page content or browser state through CDP, outside ordinary navigation or UI interaction, and leave that change in place, tell the user what changed in the final response.\n\n```ts\nconst capability = await tab.capabilities.get(\"cdp\");\n\ntype CdpEventsOptions = {\n  afterSequence?: number; // Return events after this cursor; omit to start at the current position.\n  limit?: number; // Maximum number of events to return, from 1 to 1000.\n  methods?: Array<string>; // Return only these CDP event methods; must not be empty.\n  target?: CdpTarget; // Filter by child target, including buffered events after it detaches.\n  timeoutMs?: number; // Wait up to this many milliseconds for the first match.\n};\n\ntype CdpCommandParams = Record<string, unknown>;\n\ntype CdpSendOptions = {\n  target?: CdpTarget; // An attached child target; omit to send the command to the tab itself.\n  timeoutMs?: number; // Maximum command wait in milliseconds.\n};\n\ntype CdpTarget = { sessionId: string; targetId?: never } | { sessionId?: never; targetId: string };\n\ninterface CdpTabCapability {\n  readEvents(options?: CdpEventsOptions): Promise<{ cursor: number; events: Array<{ method: string; params?: Record<string, unknown>; sequence: number; source: { extensionId?: string; sessionId?: string; tabId?: number; targetId?: string } }>; hasMore: boolean; truncated: boolean }>; // Read buffered CDP events, optionally waiting for the first match.\n  send(method: string, params?: CdpCommandParams, options?: CdpSendOptions): Promise<unknown>; // Send a permitted CDP command to this tab or an attached child target.\n}\n```\n"}],"isError":false,"_meta":{"codex/nodeReplExecutionDurationMs":1}},"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":4584125}},"started_at_ms":1788573155380,"completed_at_ms":1788573155385}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-05T01:52:35.388Z","ordinal":20887,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a06f44-803c-76c3-b924-65774cdf788b","call_id":"call_HdhSiquXNWHG5FYz2W7ep0IQ","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Wall time: 0.0069 seconds\nOutput:"},{"type":"input_text","text":"# Tab Capability: cdp\nRaw Chrome DevTools Protocol access in browser for development use. Prefer higher-level Browser Use APIs. Navigate a fresh tab to its intended HTTP or HTTPS page before the first CDP command. Raw CDP access is scoped to the tab's current web origin. To observe an action, call `readEvents()` to capture `cursor`, perform the action, then read from that cursor with `afterSequence`. Continue from each returned cursor while `hasMore` is true; `truncated` means older events were evicted. Reuse the same filters while paging. Discover child target selectors from `Target.attachedToTarget` events. If you directly modify page content or browser state through CDP, outside ordinary navigation or UI interaction, and leave that change in place, tell the user what changed in the final response.\n\n```ts\nconst capability = await tab.capabilities.get(\"cdp\");\n\ntype CdpEventsOptions = {\n  afterSequence?: number; // Return events after this cursor; omit to start at the current position.\n  limit?: number; // Maximum number of events to return, from 1 to 1000.\n  methods?: Array<string>; // Return only these CDP event methods; must not be empty.\n  target?: CdpTarget; // Filter by child target, including buffered events after it detaches.\n  timeoutMs?: number; // Wait up to this many milliseconds for the first match.\n};\n\ntype CdpCommandParams = Record<string, unknown>;\n\ntype CdpSendOptions = {\n  target?: CdpTarget; // An attached child target; omit to send the command to the tab itself.\n  timeoutMs?: number; // Maximum command wait in milliseconds.\n};\n\ntype CdpTarget = { sessionId: string; targetId?: never } | { sessionId?: never; targetId: string };\n\ninterface CdpTabCapability {\n  readEvents(options?: CdpEventsOptions): Promise<{ cursor: number; events: Array<{ method: string; params?: Record<string, unknown>; sequence: number; source: { extensionId?: string; sessionId?: string; tabId?: number; targetId?: string } }>; hasMore: boolean; truncated: boolean }>; // Read buffered CDP events, optionally waiting for the first match.\n  send(method: string, params?: CdpCommandParams, options?: CdpSendOptions): Promise<unknown>; // Send a permitted CDP command to this tab or an attached child target.\n}\n```\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a06cdc-6399-7b30-9fa8-4b87f0cfba0e","create_time":1788573155.388853}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":30000}}
