"added\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"removed\\\": 40\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"identity\\\": {\\n    \\\"owningPaths\\\": 6,\\n    \\\"parentFiles\\\": 1304,\\n    \\\"outputFiles\\\": 1305,\\n    \\\"unchangedContextFiles\\\": 1299,\\n    \\\"everyParentHashAndModeMatchesFinal17B\\\": true,\\n    \\\"everyOwningPreimageAndPostimageHashAndModeMatchesManifest\\\": true,\\n    \\\"bothProjectionStreamsReproduced\\\": true\\n  },\\n  \\\"sourceReview\\\": [\\n    \\\"Read full six-path delta against exact final17B. Only ordinary events.update, its exclusive option schema/group membership, lifecycle callback and exclusive rollback helper/import retire; release note matches this boundary.\\\",\\n    \\\"The complete events.updateGraph schema declaration and handler suffix are byte-identical to final17B. Its EventsUpdateRpcError union remains. findOneForEdit stays available.\\\",\\n    \\\"Platform contract, handler, live component call and endpoint inventory are untouched and retain platform.events.update. Literal searches found no remaining ordinary events.update or exclusive schema symbol in captured runtime/test/helper sources.\\\",\\n    \\\"Four replacement scenarios target the surviving graph API: invalid dates before SQL; invalid registration window and simple graph shape with BEGIN/ROLLBACK; tax rejection against the locked replacement Stripe account with exact lock/write/role/tax/rollback sequence. Each asserts no option write where applicable.\\\",\\n    \\\"The new fixture uses the real shared Drizzle SQL layer with inferred GraphUpdateInput, full RPC metadata and schema-derived rows; named expected queries check tenant/event/account parameters and unexpected statements fail. No new casts bypass the contract.\\\",\\n    \\\"The Stripe create source guard changes only its next-handler delimiter; all serialization assertions remain. The endpoint inventory removes only ordinary events.update.\\\",\\n    \\\"Newer ESN create/mapping, generated option-ID, template defaults, announcement role defaults, transfer/check-in and discovery outputs remain in the inherited code/test context; all1299 non-owning files are byte/mode-identical.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"supportingReviews\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"independent-review/receipt.json\\\",\\n      \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"8d65a15d5744ff3a55f15203ac7f27964b8e89a2d5d1cb0c3ee3dbbb39146cff\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"independent-review/test-preservation.json\\\",\\n      \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"9d468adefd9c1ed931a57a60504d6705126a4de39dcee0b90acdd7a4c5cb8324\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"independent-review/source-identities.json\\\",\\n      \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"687d0645f68b5b685a17bc38d6674440161c6bf63f29b7a6799ce4ca9db63b19\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"coordination\\\": \\\"Reused the completed nested source review and read its evidence; no new agent or duplicate runtime review dispatched. Performed independent full diff and hash/mode/endpoint checks requested by root.\\\",\\n  \\\"limitations\\\": [\\n    \\\"Source-only acceptance; no compiler, lint/format, unit, PostgreSQL, browser, runtime, provider, network or ref action.\\\",\\n    \\\"The fixture assertions are reviewed source coverage, not executed results. Actual-parent materialization and canonical gates remain pending.\\\",\\n    \\\"Existing source, plans, patches and review receipts remain unchanged; only this separate review artifact was written.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"concreteDefects\\\": []\\n}\\n# Ordinary legacy event API retirement\\n\\nThis six-path source projection removes the authenticated ordinary events.update endpoint and its private input schema/handler after the discovery layer. No first-party client calls it. Its inherited role-lock-before-event-row order was documented in17B; the surviving graph update keeps its existing event-row-first implementation. The distinct platform.events.update API remains intact.\\n\\nFour prior behavior scenarios now run against the surviving graph endpoint with typed database/RPC fixtures: date preflight, invalid registration windows, invalid simple graph shape, and payment-account drift. Transactional cases assert rollback, no commit, and no option write; they do not pretend validation happens before loading the graph. Every other current create/discovery/review case remains.\\n\\nThe exact final17B source projection is captured as parent; actual branch identity and canonical proof remain pending. The original six-path proposal, original capture and separate endpoint-order predecessor correction remain immutable. No public-detail projection or unrelated cleanup belongs to this layer.\\nRemove the unused ordinary events.update contract, input schema and handler so event editing has one graph update path. The separate platform update API remains supported. This also removes the documented inherited lock-order inversion in the old handler.\\n\\nRetain the old date, registration-window, graph-shape and account-drift behavior obligations as typed graph-update scenarios, with rollback and no option writes on rejection. Update only the owning handler inventory and source boundary guard.\\n\\nSource review only; actual-head canonical, strict, unit and PostgreSQL evidence remains pending.\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":1,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"071353\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000002042,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2048,\"output\":\"--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/.changeset/retire-legacy-event-update.md\\n@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\\n+---\\n+\\\"evorto\\\": patch\\n+---\\n+\\n+Remove the legacy ordinary `events.update` API. Event editing continues through `events.updateGraph`, including date, registration, permission and payment validation. The platform event update API remains available.\\n--- a/src/server/effect/rpc/handlers/events/events-lifecycle.handlers.spec.ts\\n+++ b/src/server/effect/rpc/handlers/events/events-lifecycle.handlers.spec.ts\\n@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@\\n+import type * as SqlConnection from 'effect/unstable/sql/SqlConnection';\\n+\\n import { describe, expect, it } from '@effect/vitest';\\n import { createDatabaseTestLayer } from '@server/testing/database-test-layer';\\n-import { TransactionRollbackError } from 'drizzle-orm';\\n import { Effect, Layer } from 'effect';\\n import * as Headers from 'effect/unstable/http/Headers';\\n import { Rpc, RpcMessage } from 'effect/unstable/rpc';\\n@@ -22,7 +23,10 @@\\n   RpcRequestContextMiddleware,\\n   type RpcRequestContextShape,\\n } from '../../../../../shared/rpc-contracts/app-rpcs';\\n-import { EventsUpdateAnnouncementDiscovery } from '../../../../../shared/rpc-contracts/app-rpcs/events.rpcs';\\n+import {\\n+  EventsUpdateAnnouncementDiscovery,\\n+  EventsUpdateGraph,\\n+} from '../../../../../shared/rpc-contracts/app-rpcs/events.rpcs';\\n import { createRegistrationDatabaseTestLayer } from '../../../../testing/registration-database';\\n import { RpcAccess } from '../shared/rpc-access.service';\\n import {\\n@@ -146,6 +150,230 @@\\n     ...option,\\n     id: 'option-1',\\n   })),\\n+};\\n+\\n+type GraphUpdateInput = Parameters<\\n+  (typeof eventLifecycleHandlers)['events.updateGraph']\\n+>[0];\\n+type GraphSqlCall = (\\n+  ...args: Parameters<SqlConnection.Connection['executeValues']>\\n+) => void;\\n+\\n+const graphUpdateInput = {\\n+  addOns: [],\\n+  description: updateInput.description,\\n+  end: updateInput.end,\\n+  eventId: updateInput.eventId,\\n+  icon: updateInput.icon,\\n+  location: updateInput.location,\\n+  questions: [],\\n+  registrationOptions: updateInput.registrationOptions.flatMap((option) => [\\n+    {\\n+      ...option,\\n+      esnCardDiscountedPrice: null,\\n+      key: option.id,\\n+    },\\n+    {\\n+      ...option,\\n+      esnCardDiscountedPrice: null,\\n+      id: 'organizer-1',\\n+      key: 'organizer-1',\\n+      organizingRegistration: true,\\n+      title: 'Organizer',\\n+    },\\n+  ]),\\n+  simpleModeEnabled: false,\\n+  start: updateInput.start,\\n+  title: updateInput.title,\\n+} satisfies GraphUpdateInput;\\n+\\n+const graphUpdateRpcOptions = () => ({\\n+  client: new Rpc.ServerClient(1),\\n+  headers: Headers.empty,\\n+  requestId: RpcMessage.RequestId(1),\\n+  rpc: EventsUpdateGraph.middleware(RpcRequestContextMiddleware),\\n+});\\n+\\n+const graphDatabaseTimestamp = (value: Date) =>\\n+  value.toISOString().replace('T', ' ').replace('Z', '');\\n+\\n+const createGraphUpdateDatabase = ({\\n+  simpleModeEnabled = false,\\n+}: {\\n+  simpleModeEnabled?: boolean;\\n+} = {}) => {\\n+  const event = {\\n+    creatorId: user.id,\\n+    description: graphUpdateInput.description,\\n+    end: new Date(graphUpdateInput.end),\\n+    icon: graphUpdateInput.icon,\\n+    id: graphUpdateInput.eventId,\\n+    location: graphUpdateInput.location,\\n+    simpleModeEnabled,\\n+    start: new Date(graphUpdateInput.start),\\n+    status: 'DRAFT',\\n+    title: graphUpdateInput.title,\\n+  } satisfies Pick<\\n+    typeof eventInstances.$inferSelect,\\n+    | 'creatorId'\\n+    | 'description'\\n+    | 'end'\\n+    | 'icon'\\n+    | 'id'\\n+    | 'location'\\n+    | 'simpleModeEnabled'\\n+    | 'start'\\n+    | 'status'\\n+    | 'title'\\n+  >;\\n+  const options = graphUpdateInput.registrationOptions.map((option) => ({\\n+    cancellationDeadlineHoursBeforeStart:\\n+      option.cancellationDeadlineHoursBeforeStart,\\n+    closeRegistrationTime: new Date(option.closeRegistrationTime),\\n+    description: option.description,\\n+    id: option.id,\\n+    isPaid: option.isPaid,\\n+    openRegistrationTime: new Date(option.openRegistrationTime),\\n+    organizingRegistration: option.organizingRegistration,\\n+    price: option.price,\\n+    refundFeesOnCancellation: option.refundFeesOnCancellation,\\n+    registeredDescription: option.registeredDescription,\\n+    registrationMode: option.registrationMode,\\n+    roleIds: option.roleIds,\\n+    spots: option.spots,\\n+    stripeTaxRateId: option.stripeTaxRateId,\\n+    title: option.title,\\n+    transferDeadlineHoursBeforeStart:\\n+      option.transferDeadlineHoursBeforeStart,\\n+  }) satisfies Pick<\\n+    typeof eventRegistrationOptions.$inferSelect,\\n+    | 'cancellationDeadlineHoursBeforeStart'\\n+    | 'closeRegistrationTime'\\n+    | 'description'\\n+    | 'id'\\n+    | 'isPaid'\\n+    | 'openRegistrationTime'\\n+    | 'organizingRegistration'\\n+    | 'price'\\n+    | 'refundFeesOnCancellation'\\n+    | 'registeredDescription'\\n+    | 'registrationMode'\\n+    | 'roleIds'\\n+    | 'spots'\\n+    | 'stripeTaxRateId'\\n+    | 'title'\\n+    | 'transferDeadlineHoursBeforeStart'\\n+  >);\\n+  const sqlCalls = vi.fn<GraphSqlCall>();\\n+  const eventWrites = vi.fn<GraphSqlCall>();\\n+  const optionWrites = vi.fn<GraphSqlCall>();\\n+  const operationOrder: string[] = [];\\n+  const transactionCommands: string[] = [];\\n+  const databaseLayer = createRegistrationDatabaseTestLayer({\\n+    executeValues: (statement, parameters) => Effect.sync(() => {\\n+      sqlCalls(statement, parameters);\\n+      if (statement.startsWith('select \\\"d0\\\".\\\"creatorId\\\" as \\\"creatorId\\\", \\\"d0\\\".\\\"status\\\" as \\\"status\\\"')) {\\n+        expect(statement).toContain('from \\\"event_instances\\\" as \\\"d0\\\"');\\n+        expect(statement).toContain('\\\"d0\\\".\\\"id\\\" = $1');\\n+        expect(statement).toContain('\\\"d0\\\".\\\"tenantId\\\" = $2');\\n+        expect(parameters).toEqual([event.id, tenant.id, 1]);\\n+        return [[event.creatorId, event.status]];\\n+      }\\n+      if (statement === 'select \\\"stripeAccountId\\\" from \\\"tenants\\\" where \\\"tenants\\\".\\\"id\\\" = $1 for update') {\\n+        expect(parameters).toEqual([tenant.id]);\\n+        operationOrder.push('lock-account');\\n+        return [['acct_replacement']];\\n+      }\\n+      if (statement.startsWith('select \\\"id\\\" from \\\"event_instances\\\"') && statement.endsWith(' for update')) {\\n+        expect(statement).toContain('\\\"event_instances\\\".\\\"id\\\" = $1');\\n+        expect(statement).toContain('\\\"event_instances\\\".\\\"tenantId\\\" = $2');\\n+        expect(statement).toContain('\\\"event_instances\\\".\\\"status\\\" = $3');\\n+        expect(parameters).toEqual([event.id, tenant.id, 'DRAFT']);\\n+        operationOrder.push('lock-event');\\n+        return [[event.id]];\\n+      }\\n+      if (statement.startsWith('select \\\"description\\\", \\\"end\\\", \\\"icon\\\", \\\"id\\\", \\\"location\\\", \\\"simpleModeEnabled\\\", \\\"start\\\", \\\"title\\\" from \\\"event_instances\\\"')) {\\n+        expect(statement).toContain('\\\"event_instances\\\".\\\"id\\\" = $1');\\n+        expect(statement).toContain('\\\"event_instances\\\".\\\"tenantId\\\" = $2');\\n+        expect(parameters).toEqual([event.id, tenant.id, 1]);\\n+        return [[event.description, graphDatabaseTimestamp(event.end), event.icon, event.id, event.location, event.simpleModeEnabled, graphDatabaseTimestamp(event.start), event.title]];\\n+      }\\n+      if (statement.includes('from \\\"event_registration_options\\\" inner join \\\"event_instances\\\"')) {\\n+        expect(statement).toContain('\\\"event_registration_options\\\".\\\"eventId\\\" = $1');\\n+        expect(statement).toContain('\\\"event_instances\\\".\\\"tenantId\\\" = $2');\\n+        expect(parameters).toEqual([event.id, tenant.id]);\\n+        return options.map((option) => [\\n+          option.cancellationDeadlineHoursBeforeStart,\\n+          graphDatabaseTimestamp(option.closeRegistrationTime),\\n+          option.description,\\n+          option.id,\\n+          option.isPaid,\\n+          graphDatabaseTimestamp(option.openRegistrationTime),\\n+          option.organizingRegistration,\\n+          option.price,\\n+          option.refundFeesOnCancellation,\\n+          option.registeredDescription,\\n+          option.registrationMode,\\n+          option.roleIds,\\n+          option.spots,\\n+          option.stripeTaxRateId,\\n+          option.title,\\n+          option.transferDeadlineHoursBeforeStart,\\n+        ]);\\n+      }\\n+      if (statement.startsWith('select ') && statement.includes('from \\\"event_registration_option_discounts\\\"')) {\\n+        expect(parameters).toEqual(['esnCard', ...options.map((option) => option.id)]);\\n+        return [];\\n+      }\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":2,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"7dd614\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000001417,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1173,\"output\":\"{\\n  \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"2026-09-05T01:45:43.484553+00:00\\\",\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"sealed source-only final-parent projection; actual heads and canonical gates pending\\\",\\n  \\\"pathCount\\\": 6,\\n  \\\"insertions\\\": 314,\\n  \\\"deletions\\\": 588,\\n  \\\"parentCommit\\\": null,\\n  \\\"parent17BManifestSha256\\\": \\\"4f4c6eacadeb4cb125d96e953ea5ee94c66fe5634ba9cab6248dbf2c7471a75e\\\",\\n  \\\"parent17BPatchSha256\\\": \\\"927d18772238ce888282f4eec010862769755f4319d5eba980e2ac6215fdabdf\\\",\\n  \\\"parentProjectionSha256\\\": \\\"9051554e7df4830e8cc7b135d58c099388aa7a4d6b462a574b517244daa96dff\\\",\\n  \\\"inputAuthoritySha256\\\": \\\"fc7e39f8cfea39306fe28813982d85cfc506b984bb1c00e5514fbc98d0e23421\\\",\\n  \\\"compositionLedgerSha256\\\": \\\"d9eec50aea26ccaf892edb78bd9f3857d8658666d08f60da371db07b340e579e\\\",\\n  \\\"capturedInputFileCount\\\": 1304,\\n  \\\"outputFileCount\\\": 1305,\\n  \\\"unchangedContextFileCount\\\": 1299,\\n  \\\"outputProjectionSha256\\\": \\\"f218406d79f4a8a2f39f16cede420043322608a6a2fdf32d582f5b467b9f0bcf\\\",\\n  \\\"projectionSerialization\\\": \\\"Python pathlib.PurePosixPath component-wise order of relative POSIX paths; UTF-8 path + NUL + SHA256 + NUL + four-octal mode + LF\\\",\\n  \\\"patchSha256\\\": \\\"ee571cd76008735cc3e487fa490b6f6ab90df9926d53296018322a94569fe2a7\\\",\\n  \\\"candidatePatchSha256\\\": \\\"ee571cd76008735cc3e487fa490b6f6ab90df9926d53296018322a94569fe2a7\\\",\\n  \\\"files