n proves that application, server, schema, dependencies and build inputs are unchanged. The [runtime receipt](assembly-4dd644-runtime-gates.json) records both identities and all log hashes. The complete combined documentation publication also passes54/54 and installs13 guides into an isolated Pages checkout. Its 19 tooling tests, lint, diff check and production build pass under the separate pinned Pages runtime (Node 24.11.0/Bun 1.3.14). The installed catalog contains 13 guides and 199 PNGs with 203 references, no missing or unused images, and no retired output. Search and guide navigation work in the production preview, and the neutral email crop passes visual review. Final visual acceptance remains held: F-229 records a stale prior approval notification in the missing-file receipt screenshot. A separate companion anchor-offset issue is under review. The exact installed output has a verified local archive. That prior owned app runtime has now been stopped and its exact project resources removed.\n\nThe preceding implementation checkpoint is `c5f8a1b10a6e03a896dad7694c57c851c61f6d4c` (33 changed paths). Payment review copy, normalized copied transfer codes, locked check-in timing, transferred add-on reads, copied paid-template checks and fixture ownership repairs pass 1,674 server tests, 1,172 app tests and 123 PostgreSQL tests. The final 24-root strict graph has zero diagnostics. Exact source hashes retain the earlier app/PG results across the last test-only additions, and database readback confirms no owned RLS objects or fixture tenants remain. [Clean source receipt](assembly-ticket-fixture-final-source.json). Its production runtime is the verified source-equivalent runtime for the complete 4dd644 acceptance above.\n\nThe previous complete runtime checkpoint is the clean assembly head `5d49f011c4d6f467c3d74d0241b99173f5a6f87f`. It adds audit-specific microsecond cursors, readable audit descriptions, effective role details and a durable wildcard rename/revocation 